C · bit-fields · fit-and-alternatives · L3
Concept: Pack fields into integers with shifts and masks when the layout must be portable
Misconception: Adding the fields together packs them into one byte.
Explanation: Shifts and masks fix the layout on every compiler. Mask each input to its width before shifting it into place, or an oversized value spills into the neighboring field. Unpack with a shift followed by a mask.
Incorrect:
unsigned packBad(unsigned hi, unsigned lo) { return (hi << 4) + lo; }
Correct:
uint8_t pack(unsigned hi, unsigned lo) { return (uint8_t)(((hi & 0xFu) << 4) | (lo & 0xFu)); }
unsigned hiNibble(uint8_t b) { return (b >> 4) & 0xFu; }
unsigned loNibble(uint8_t b) { return b & 0xFu; }
Complexity: O(1)

