C · disjoint sets (union-find) · access · L2
Concept: Find the root, then point every node on the path directly at it (path compression)
Misconception: find only reads the parent array, so it should not change it.
Explanation: Path compression makes find rewrite the parent of every node it visits to the root, so later finds on those nodes take one step. The iterative version runs two passes: one to locate the root and one to relink. Without compression a chain of n nodes costs O(n) for every find. With compression and union by rank the amortised cost per operation is O(alpha(n)), effectively constant.
Incorrect:
size_t findNoCompress(const size_t *p, size_t x) {
  while (p[x] != x) x = p[x];
  return x;
}
Correct:
size_t dsFind(DSU *d, size_t x) {
  if (x >= d->n) return DS_NONE;
  size_t root = x;
  while (d->p[root] != root) root = d->p[root];
  while (d->p[x] != root) {
    size_t next = d->p[x];
    d->p[x] = root;
    x = next;
  }
  return root;
}
Complexity: O(alpha(n))

