C · disjoint sets (union-find) · mutation · L3
Concept: Union links the two roots, attaching the shallower tree under the deeper one (union by rank)
Misconception: Union can set parent[a] = b directly for the two elements.
Explanation: Setting the parent of a non-root element detaches it from the rest of its set: other members that pointed through it are cut off from the new set. Union must find both roots first. Linking the lower-rank root under the higher-rank root keeps the trees shallow, and the rank grows only when the two ranks are equal.
Incorrect:
void unionBad(size_t *p, size_t a, size_t b) { p[a] = b; }
Correct:
int dsUnion(DSU *d, size_t a, size_t b) {
  size_t ra = dsFind(d, a), rb = dsFind(d, b);
  if (ra == DS_NONE || rb == DS_NONE || ra == rb) return 0;
  if (d->rank[ra] < d->rank[rb]) { size_t t = ra; ra = rb; rb = t; }
  d->p[rb] = ra;
  if (d->rank[ra] == d->rank[rb]) d->rank[ra]++;
  d->count--;
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(alpha(n))

