C · dynamic arrays · patterns · L2
Concept: Binary search the half-open range [lo, hi); with a closed range and unsigned indexes the empty and past-the-end cases break
Misconception: Use hi = n - 1 and return lo when the loop ends.
Explanation: lower_bound returns the first index whose value is not less than the key, which is n when every element is smaller. With hi = n - 1 the answer can never be n, and for n = 0 the unsigned n - 1 wraps. Use hi = n, the loop while lo < hi, and mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2.
Incorrect:
size_t lowerBoundBad(const int *a, size_t n, int key) {
  size_t lo = 0, hi = n - 1;
  while (lo < hi) {
    size_t mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
    if (a[mid] < key) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid;
  }
  return lo;
}
Correct:
size_t lowerBound(const int *a, size_t n, int key) {
  size_t lo = 0, hi = n;
  while (lo < hi) {
    size_t mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
    if (a[mid] < key) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid;
  }
  return lo;
}
Complexity: O(log n)

