C · enum · patterns · L3
Concept: Use powers of two for flag enums so values combine with | and test with &
Misconception: Sequential enumerators 1, 2, 3 work as combinable flags.
Explanation: Bit flags need one bit each: 1, 2, 4, 8. With 1, 2, 3 the value 3 equals 1 | 2, so a combination cannot be told from a single flag. Combine with |, clear with & ~flag and test with (flags & f) == f.
Incorrect:
enum PermBad { PB_R = 1, PB_W = 2, PB_X = 3 };
int hasBad(int flags, int f) { return (flags & f) == f; }
Correct:
enum Perm { PERM_R = 1, PERM_W = 2, PERM_X = 4 };
int has(int flags, int f) { return (flags & f) == f; }
Complexity: O(1)

