C · enum · patterns · L2
Concept: Switch over an enum without a default so the compiler warns about missing cases
Misconception: A switch over an enum only needs the cases you care about.
Explanation: With -Wall gcc reports every enumerator missing from a switch that has no default (-Wswitch). That turns adding a new enumerator into a list of places to update. Handle every value in the switch and put the fallback after it for invalid integers.
Incorrect (compiles with a warning: not handled in switch):
enum Color { RED, GREEN, BLUE };
const char *nameBad(enum Color c) {
  switch (c) {
    case RED: return "red";
    case GREEN: return "green";
  }
  return "?";
