C · enum · mental-model · L1
Concept: Enumerators start at 0 and each one is the previous plus one, unless given a value
Misconception: Each constant in an enum is numbered from 1 unless told otherwise.
Explanation: Without explicit values the first enumerator is 0 and every next one is the previous plus 1. An explicit value changes the counter: enum { LOW = 1, MID, HIGH = 10, MAX } gives 1, 2, 10 and 11. Enumerators are int constants usable in array sizes and case labels.
Incorrect:
enum LevelBad { LOW_B = 1, MID_B, HIGH_B = 10, MAX_B };
