C · intbits · mutation · L2
Concept: uint8_t arithmetic is done in int, so a + b < a never detects a wrap
Misconception: a + b < a detects overflow of two uint8_t values.
Explanation: Operands narrower than int are promoted to int before arithmetic. 200 + 100 is 300 in an int, which is not less than 200. Convert the sum back to uint8_t before comparing: (uint8_t)(a + b) < a is true when the 8-bit sum wrapped.
Incorrect:
bool wrapsBad(uint8_t a, uint8_t b) {
  return a + b < a;
}
Correct:
bool wraps8(uint8_t a, uint8_t b) {
  return (uint8_t)(a + b) < a;
}
Complexity: O(1)

