C · queues · access · L1
Concept: Dequeue returns the oldest element and must refuse an empty queue
Misconception: Dequeue can decrement the length without checking it.
Explanation: The element at data[head] is the oldest. Advance head with the same modulo, shrink len, and return a status because an empty queue has nothing to give. Without the check len wraps from 0 to the maximum value and the queue reports that it is full of garbage.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { int *data; size_t head, len, cap; } Queue;
int dequeueBad(Queue *q) {
  int v = q->data[q->head];
  q->head = (q->head + 1) % q->cap;
  q->len--;
  return v;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { int *data; size_t head, len, cap; } Queue;
int dequeue(Queue *q, int *out) {
  if (q->len == 0) return 0;
  *out = q->data[q->head];
  q->head = (q->head + 1) % q->cap;
  q->len--;
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

