C · segment trees · edge-cases · L3
Concept: Sums of int values can overflow int; accumulate in long long
Misconception: A range sum of int values fits in an int.
Explanation: Two values near INT_MAX already overflow int, and signed overflow is undefined behaviour that UBSan reports. Store and return node sums as long long, as the tree here does, or as unsigned types when the problem says so. Widening happens before the addition, not after.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: signed integer overflow):
int rangeSumBad(const int *a, size_t n) {
  int s = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) s += a[i];
  return s;
}
Correct:
long long rangeSumWide(const int *a, size_t n) {
  long long s = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) s += a[i];
  return s;
}
Complexity: O(n)

