C · stacks · patterns · L2
Concept: Match brackets with a stack of open brackets; counting parentheses cannot check order or kinds
Misconception: A string is balanced if it has as many ( as ) characters.
Explanation: The string )( has equal counts but is not balanced, and ([)] mixes kinds in the wrong order. Push each open bracket, and for each close bracket pop and compare the kind. The string is balanced if no mismatch occurs and the stack is empty at the end. Time O(n), extra space O(n).
Incorrect:
int balancedBad(const char *s) {
  int d = 0;
  for (; *s != '\0'; s++) {
    if (*s == '(') d++;
    else if (*s == ')') d--;
  }
  return d == 0;
}
Correct:
int balanced(const char *s) {
  size_t top = 0;
  char *st = malloc(strlen(s) + 1);
  if (st == NULL) return 0;
  int ok = 1;
  for (size_t i = 0; s[i] != '\0' && ok; i++) {
    char c = s[i];
    if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {
      st[top++] = c;
    } else if (c == ')' || c == ']' || c == '}') {
      char open = c == ')' ? '(' : (c == ']' ? '[' : '{');
      if (top == 0 || st[--top] != open) ok = 0;
    }
  }
  free(st);
  return ok && top == 0;
}
Complexity: O(n)

