C · stacks · access · L1
Concept: Report an empty stack from pop instead of decrementing the length below zero
Misconception: Popping an empty stack returns the last value that was there.
Explanation: len is unsigned, so --len on an empty stack wraps to the maximum value and the next access is far outside the array. Return a status code and write the value through an out-parameter, and give peek the same check. Pop and peek are O(1).
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow):
typedef struct { int *data; size_t len, cap; } Stack;
int stackPopBad(Stack *s) { return s->data[--s->len]; }
Correct:
typedef struct { int *data; size_t len, cap; } Stack;
int stackPop(Stack *s, int *out) {
  if (s->len == 0) return 0;
  *out = s->data[--s->len];
  return 1;
}
int stackPeek(const Stack *s, int *out) {
  if (s->len == 0) return 0;
  *out = s->data[s->len - 1];
  return 1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

