C · struct · equality · L2
Concept: Structs cannot be compared with ==; compare member by member
Misconception: a == b compares two structs field by field.
Explanation: The == operator is not defined for struct types, so the compiler rejects it. Comparing the bytes with memcmp is also unreliable because the padding bytes are indeterminate. Compare the members one by one in a small function.
Incorrect (does not compile: invalid operands):
struct Q { int x; int y; };
int eqBad(struct Q a, struct Q b) { return a == b; }
Correct:
struct Q { int x; int y; };
int eqQ(struct Q a, struct Q b) { return a.x == b.x && a.y == b.y; }
Complexity: O(1)

