C · time and date structures · mutation · L2
Concept: gmtime and localtime return a shared static struct; use the _r variants
Misconception: Two calls to gmtime give two independent results.
Explanation: gmtime and localtime return a pointer to one static struct tm that every later call overwrites, so keeping two results leaves both pointers showing the last time. They are also not thread safe. gmtime_r and localtime_r fill a struct you provide.
Incorrect:
int sameYearBad(time_t a, time_t b) {
  struct tm *x = gmtime(&a);
  struct tm *y = gmtime(&b);
  return x->tm_year == y->tm_year;
}
Correct:
int sameYear(time_t a, time_t b) {
  struct tm x, y;
  gmtime_r(&a, &x);
  gmtime_r(&b, &y);
  return x.tm_year == y.tm_year;
}
Complexity: O(1)

