Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · adc and dac sampling · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Reject spikes with a median of three instead of an average
Misconception: Averaging three readings removes a noise spike.
Explanation: A single wrong sample (an electrical spike, a missed conversion) shifts an average by a third of its size. The median of three returns the middle value and ignores one outlier completely. It needs only comparisons, no wide accumulator, and it keeps the original resolution.
Incorrect:
uint16_t meanBad(uint16_t a, uint16_t b, uint16_t c) {
  return (uint16_t)(((uint32_t)a + b + c) / 3U);
}
Correct:
uint16_t median3(uint16_t a, uint16_t b, uint16_t c) {
  if (a > b) { uint16_t t = a; a = b; b = t; }
  if (b > c) { b = c; }
  return a > b ? a : b;
}
Complexity: O(1)

