Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · adc and dac sampling · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Oversample 4^n readings in a 32-bit sum and shift right by n to gain n bits
Misconception: Averaging N readings in a 16-bit variable is enough.
Explanation: Adding 64 readings of up to 4095 reaches 262080, which wraps a 16-bit accumulator. Sum into a uint32_t. Dividing the sum by N gives an average with the same 12 bits; shifting right by n after summing 4^n readings keeps extra resolution (64 readings and a shift of 3 give 15 bits). The gain exists only if the input has noise of about one LSB to dither the readings.
Incorrect:
uint16_t overBad(const uint16_t *s, unsigned n) {
  uint16_t sum = 0;
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += s[i];
  return sum >> 3;
}
Correct:
uint32_t oversample(const uint16_t *s, unsigned n, unsigned shift) {
  uint32_t sum = 0;
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += s[i];
  return sum >> shift;
}
Complexity: O(n)

