Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · adc and dac sampling · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Fill a DAC waveform table so the last entry reaches full scale (divide by n - 1)
Misconception: buf[i] = i * 4095 / n gives a full ramp from 0 to 4095.
Explanation: With n entries the indexes run from 0 to n - 1, so the step for the last entry must divide by n - 1 to reach 4095. Dividing by n stops one step short (3276 of 4095 for five entries). The table length is a buffer size, so writing buf[n] to "reach the end" writes one element past the array, which AddressSanitizer reports.
Incorrect:
void rampBad(uint16_t *buf, unsigned n) {
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++)
    buf[i] = (uint16_t)(i * 4095U / n);
}
Correct:
void rampFill(uint16_t *buf, unsigned n) {
  for (unsigned i = 0; i < n; i++)
    buf[i] = n > 1 ? (uint16_t)(i * 4095U / (n - 1U)) : 0;
}
Complexity: O(n)

