Context: platform: AVR_Bare_Metal
Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr gpio registers · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Enable the pull-up of an input by clearing its DDR bit and setting its PORT bit
Misconception: Setting the PORT bit is enough to get a pull-up.
Explanation: The same PORTx bit means different things by direction: on an output it sets the level, on an input it enables the pull-up resistor. If the pin is still an output (DDR bit 1) the PORT write only drives it high. Clear the DDR bit first, then set the PORT bit. A pressed button wired to ground then reads 0.
Incorrect:
void inputPullupBad(uint8_t bit) {
  PORTB |= (1 << bit);
}
Correct:
void inputPullup(uint8_t bit) {
  DDRB &= ~(1 << bit);
  PORTB |= (1 << bit);
}
Complexity: O(1)

