Context: platform: AVR_Bare_Metal
Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr usart spi and twi · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Configure the SPI master with SS as an output so the hardware cannot fall back to slave mode
Misconception: MOSI and SCK need to be outputs; SS can be ignored in master mode.
Explanation: On the ATmega328P, if SS (PB2) is an input and something pulls it low, the SPI hardware assumes another master is talking and clears MSTR, turning the port into a slave. Keep SS an output (even when you use another pin for chip select). MOSI (PB3) and SCK (PB5) must be outputs and MISO (PB4) stays an input. SPCR then enables SPI (SPE), master mode (MSTR) and a clock divider (SPR bits).
Incorrect:
void spiInitBad(void) {
  DDRB |= (1 << PB3) | (1 << PB5);
  SPCR = (1 << SPE) | (1 << MSTR);
}
Correct:
void spiInit(void) {
