Context: platform: AVR_Bare_Metal
Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr timer1 and timer0 · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Start Timer1 in CTC mode by setting WGM12, a prescaler bit pattern, OCR1A and OCIE1A
Misconception: Setting only the clock-select bits starts the timer in CTC mode.
Explanation: The mode and the clock source live together in TCCR1B. WGM12 selects CTC (clear on compare match with OCR1A); the CS1x bits select the clock and also start the counter. With CS11 and CS10 set the prescaler is 64. Without WGM12 the timer runs in normal mode and counts to 65535 before wrapping. The compare interrupt is enabled with OCIE1A in TIMSK1 and also needs the global interrupt flag.
Incorrect:
void timerBad(uint16_t ocr) {
  OCR1A = ocr;
  TCCR1B |= (1 << CS11) | (1 << CS10);
}
Correct:
void timer1Start64(uint16_t ocr) {
  TCCR1A = 0;
  TCCR1B = (1 << WGM12) | (1 << CS11) | (1 << CS10);
  OCR1A = ocr;
  TIMSK1 |= (1 << OCIE1A);
}
Complexity: O(1)

