Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr timer1 and timer0 · transformation · Beginner
Concept: Compute OCR1A for CTC mode as F_CPU / (prescaler * freq) - 1
Misconception: The compare value is F_CPU / (prescaler * freq).
Explanation: In CTC mode the counter runs 0, 1, ..., OCR1A and then restarts, so one period lasts OCR1A + 1 timer ticks. The compare value must therefore be one less than the tick count per period. Use 32-bit arithmetic: 16000000 does not fit in the 16-bit int of an AVR. Without the minus one the interrupt rate is slightly low (996 Hz instead of 1000 Hz for a 1 kHz tick).
Incorrect:
uint16_t ocrBad(uint32_t freq, uint16_t presc) {
  return (uint16_t)(F_CPU / ((uint32_t)presc * freq));
}
Correct:
uint16_t timer1Ocr(uint32_t freq, uint16_t presc) {
  return (uint16_t)(F_CPU / ((uint32_t)presc * freq) - 1U);
}
Complexity: O(1)

