Context: platform: AVR_Bare_Metal
Embedded C · AVR_Bare_Metal · avr timer1 and timer0 · complexity · Intermediate
Concept: Set up 8-bit Fast PWM on OC0A and remember that PD6 must be an output
Misconception: Setting the compare-output mode bits is enough to get PWM on the pin.
Explanation: Fast PWM on Timer0 needs WGM01 and WGM00, COM0A1 for non-inverting output and a clock-select pattern in TCCR0B. The waveform appears on OC0A (PD6 on the ATmega328P) only if DDRD bit 6 is an output; the timer does not change the pin direction. The frequency is F_CPU / (prescaler * 256) and the duty is OCR0A / 256 of the period.
Incorrect:
void pwmBad(void) {
  TCCR0A = (1 << COM0A1) | (1 << WGM01) | (1 << WGM00);
  TCCR0B = (1 << CS01) | (1 << CS00);
}
Correct:
void pwm0Start(uint8_t duty) {
  DDRD |= (1 << PD6);
  TCCR0A = (1 << COM0A1) | (1 << WGM01) | (1 << WGM00);
  TCCR0B = (1 << CS01) | (1 << CS00);
  OCR0A = duty;
}
uint32_t fastPwmHz(uint16_t presc) {
  return F_CPU / ((uint32_t)presc * 256U);
}
Complexity: O(1)

