Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · bitwise operations · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Count set bits by clearing the lowest set bit until the value is zero
Misconception: A loop over the first 31 bit positions counts all the set bits.
Explanation: The expression x &= x - 1 clears the lowest set bit, so the loop runs once per set bit and covers all 32 bits. A loop that tests bit positions 0 to 30 forgets bit 31. Parity is the count modulo 2. Many cores have a single instruction for this and the compiler can use it through __builtin_popcount.
Incorrect:
int popBad(uint32_t x) {
  int n = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < 31; i++) n += (x >> i) & 1U;
  return n;
}
Correct:
int popCount(uint32_t x) {
  int n = 0;
  while (x) { x &= x - 1U; n++; }
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(k)

