Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · bitwise operations · creation · Beginner
Concept: Replace a multi-bit field in a register by clearing its mask first and then inserting the new value
Misconception: Setting a field is done by ORing the new value into the register.
Explanation: A field of several bits, such as a 3-bit divider code, must be cleared before the new value is inserted: reg = (reg & ~(mask << shift)) | ((value & mask) << shift). ORing without clearing leaves old bits set, and the field becomes the OR of the old and new values. Masking the value protects neighbouring fields from an oversized input.
Incorrect:
uint32_t fieldBad(uint32_t reg, unsigned shift, unsigned width, uint32_t val) {
  (void)width;
  return reg | (val << shift);
}
Correct:
uint32_t fieldSet(uint32_t reg, unsigned shift, unsigned width, uint32_t val) {
  uint32_t mask = (1U << width) - 1U;
  return (reg & ~(mask << shift)) | ((val & mask) << shift);
}
uint32_t fieldGet(uint32_t reg, unsigned shift, unsigned width) {
  return (reg >> shift) & ((1U << width) - 1U);
}
Complexity: O(1)

