Concept: Build a mask of the lowest n bits without shifting a 32-bit value by 32
Misconception: The expression (1U << n) - 1 works for every n from 0 to 32.
Explanation: Shifting a 32-bit value by 32 or more is undefined in C. For n = 32 the expression (1U << n) - 1 is therefore not safe, and on many processors the shift count is taken modulo 32, which would give 0 instead of all ones. Handle the full-width case separately.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: shift exponent):
uint32_t maskBad(unsigned n) {
  return (1U << n) - 1U;
}
Correct:
uint32_t lowMask(unsigned n) {
  return n >= 32U ? 0xFFFFFFFFU : (1U << n) - 1U;
}
Complexity: O(1)

