Concept: Sign-extend a 12-bit two-complement sensor value to a 16-bit signed integer
Misconception: A 12-bit reading stored in a 16-bit variable is already signed correctly.
Explanation: A 12-bit ADC or sensor value of 0xFFF means -1, but stored in a 16-bit integer it is 4095. The sign bit (bit 11) must be propagated. The expression (raw ^ 0x800) - 0x800 does this without relying on implementation-defined shifts of negative values.
