Embedded C · STM32_HAL · can bus · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Accept a frame when the masked identifier equals the masked filter value
Misconception: A mask filter compares the identifier directly with the filter value.
Explanation: In mask mode a filter has an id value and a mask. A 1 in the mask means that bit must match and a 0 means do not care. The test is (id & mask) == (value & mask). If the value is not masked too, any bit set in the value outside the mask makes the match fail for every frame, and the node silently receives nothing.
Incorrect:
int acceptBad(uint32_t id, uint32_t value, uint32_t mask) {
  return (id & mask) == value;
}
Correct:
int canAccept(uint32_t id, uint32_t value, uint32_t mask) {
  return (id & mask) == (value & mask);
}
Complexity: O(1)

