Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · volatile and race conditions · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Save the interrupt mask on entry and restore it on exit so critical sections can nest
Misconception: A critical section can disable interrupts at entry and enable them at exit.
Explanation: If code that is already inside a critical section calls a function that has its own, the inner exit enables interrupts too early and the rest of the outer section runs unprotected. Read PRIMASK on entry, disable interrupts, and write the saved value back on exit. The inner section then restores the already-disabled state.
Incorrect:
void enterBad(void) { __disable_irq(); }
void exitBad(void) { __enable_irq(); }
Correct:
uint32_t critEnter(void) {
  uint32_t s = __get_PRIMASK();
  __disable_irq();
  return s;
}
void critExit(uint32_t s) { __set_PRIMASK(s); }
Complexity: O(1)

