Embedded C · STM32_HAL · clock tree · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Derive the timer input clock from the bus clock, which is doubled when the APB prescaler is not 1
Misconception: A timer runs at the APB clock of its bus.
Explanation: The timers on an APB bus run at twice the bus clock whenever the APB prescaler is greater than 1, and at the bus clock when it is 1. With a 168 MHz core, APB1 divided by 4 gives 42 MHz and its timers run at 84 MHz; APB2 divided by 2 gives 84 MHz and its timers at 168 MHz. Using the bus clock gives a timer frequency that is half the real one.
Incorrect:
uint32_t timBad(uint32_t hclk, uint32_t apbDiv) {
  return hclk / apbDiv;
}
Correct:
uint32_t timClk(uint32_t hclk, uint32_t apbDiv) {
  uint32_t pclk = hclk / apbDiv;
  return apbDiv == 1 ? pclk : pclk * 2U;
}
Complexity: O(1)

