Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · crc calculation · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Compute CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE with polynomial 0x1021 and initial value 0xFFFF
Misconception: The initial value of a CRC does not matter as long as sender and receiver agree.
Explanation: The initial value matters for interoperability: CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE starts at 0xFFFF and gives 0x29B1 for 123456789, while CRC-16/XMODEM uses the same polynomial 0x1021 but starts at 0 and gives 0x31C3. A zero start also cannot detect leading zero bytes. Always name the full parameter set (width, polynomial, initial value, reflection, final XOR) when you specify a protocol.
Incorrect:
uint16_t crc16Bad(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint16_t crc = 0x0000;
  while (n--) {
    crc ^= (uint16_t)(*p++ << 8);
    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++)
      crc = (crc & 0x8000) ? (uint16_t)((crc << 1) ^ 0x1021) : (uint16_t)(crc << 1);
  }
  return crc;
}
Correct:
uint16_t crc16(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint16_t crc = 0xFFFF;
  while (n--) {
    crc ^= (uint16_t)(*p++ << 8);
    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++)
      crc = (crc & 0x8000) ? (uint16_t)((crc << 1) ^ 0x1021) : (uint16_t)(crc << 1);
  }
  return crc;
}
Complexity: O(n)

