Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · crc calculation · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Match the STM32 hardware CRC unit with CRC-32/MPEG-2 (polynomial 0x04C11DB7, no reflection)
Misconception: The STM32 hardware CRC gives the same value as the zip CRC-32.
Explanation: The default STM32 CRC unit uses polynomial 0x04C11DB7, initial value 0xFFFFFFFF, no input or output reflection and no final XOR; that is CRC-32/MPEG-2, whose check value for 123456789 is 0x0376E6E7. It differs from the zip CRC-32 (0xCBF43926). To reproduce it in software, process bits most significant first. Hardware consumes 32-bit words, so a byte stream must be fed in the same grouping on both sides.
Incorrect:
uint32_t mpeg2Bad(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  return crc32(p, n);
}
Correct:
uint32_t crcMpeg2(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint32_t crc = 0xFFFFFFFFU;
  while (n--) {
    crc ^= (uint32_t)*p++ << 24;
    for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++)
      crc = (crc & 0x80000000U) ? (crc << 1) ^ 0x04C11DB7U : crc << 1;
  }
  return crc;
}
Complexity: O(n)

