Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · checksum · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Compute Fletcher-16 with two running sums modulo 255 so that byte order matters
Misconception: Fletcher-16 reduces both sums modulo 256.
Explanation: Fletcher-16 keeps two sums: sum1 adds each byte and sum2 adds sum1 after every byte, each modulo 255. The second sum depends on position, so swapping two bytes changes the result, which a plain sum cannot see. The check value for abcde is 0xC8F0. Reducing modulo 256 instead of 255 makes the result different from the standard and weakens error detection.
Incorrect:
uint16_t fletcherBad(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint16_t a = 0, b = 0;
  while (n--) { a = (uint16_t)((a + *p++) % 256U); b = (uint16_t)((b + a) % 256U); }
  return (uint16_t)((b << 8) | a);
}
Correct:
uint16_t fletcher16(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint16_t a = 0, b = 0;
  while (n--) { a = (uint16_t)((a + *p++) % 255U); b = (uint16_t)((b + a) % 255U); }
  return (uint16_t)((b << 8) | a);
}
Complexity: O(n)

