Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · checksum · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Keep the running sums in a state object so a checksum can be updated as bytes arrive
Misconception: A checksum must be computed over the complete buffer in one call.
Explanation: In a UART receiver the bytes arrive one at a time from an interrupt. Keep the running sums in a small state structure, update it per byte, and read the result when the frame ends. Resetting the state at the start of each call, as a one-shot function does, discards the earlier bytes.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint16_t a, b; } Fl;
void flAddBad(Fl *f, uint8_t c) {
  f->a = 0; f->b = 0;
  f->a = (uint16_t)((f->a + c) % 255U);
  f->b = (uint16_t)((f->b + f->a) % 255U);
}
Correct:
typedef struct { uint16_t a, b; } Fl;
void flInit(Fl *f) { f->a = 0; f->b = 0; }
void flAdd(Fl *f, uint8_t c) {
  f->a = (uint16_t)((f->a + c) % 255U);
  f->b = (uint16_t)((f->b + f->a) % 255U);
}
uint16_t flValue(const Fl *f) { return (uint16_t)((f->b << 8) | f->a); }
Complexity: O(1)

