Context: platform: Arduino_C
Embedded C · Arduino_C · buttons and debouncing · mutation · Intermediate
Concept: Accept a new button level only after it has stayed the same for 20 ms
Misconception: Reading the pin once per loop gives one clean press per push.
Explanation: A mechanical contact bounces for a few milliseconds and the pin flips several times before it settles. A loop that reacts to every change counts each bounce as a press. Remember the last raw level and when it changed; only when the raw level has been stable for the debounce time does the stable level change.
Incorrect:
int edgesBad(const uint8_t *raw, int n) {
  int count = 0;
  for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)
    if (raw[i - 1] == 1 && raw[i] == 0) count++;
  return count;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { uint8_t raw, stable; uint32_t since; } Debounce;
void debounceInit(Debounce *d, uint8_t level) {
  d->raw = d->stable = level;
  d->since = 0;
}
uint8_t debounceUpdate(Debounce *d, uint8_t level, uint32_t now) {
  if (level != d->raw) {
    d->raw = level;
    d->since = now;
  } else if ((uint32_t)(now - d->since) >= 20U) {
    d->stable = level;
  }
  return d->stable;
}
Complexity: O(1)

