Context: platform: Arduino_C
Embedded C · Arduino_C · buttons and debouncing · edge-cases · Intermediate
Concept: Compare elapsed time with unsigned subtraction so millis() rollover is harmless
Misconception: now >= start + interval is the same as now - start >= interval.
Explanation: millis() is an unsigned 32-bit counter that wraps to 0 after about 49.7 days. start + interval can wrap while now has not, so the addition form fires immediately or never. Unsigned subtraction wraps the same way as the counter, so (uint32_t)(now - start) is the correct elapsed time across the wrap as long as the interval is shorter than half the range.
Incorrect:
int dueBad(uint32_t now, uint32_t start, uint32_t interval) {
  return now >= start + interval;
}
Correct:
int due(uint32_t now, uint32_t start, uint32_t interval) {
  return (uint32_t)(now - start) >= interval;
}
Complexity: O(1)

