Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · dma · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Compute how many unread bytes lie between the read index and the DMA write index with wrap-around
Misconception: The number of unread bytes is head minus tail.
Explanation: When DMA has wrapped past the end of the buffer, head is numerically smaller than tail and head - tail is negative; with unsigned types it becomes a huge number. Add the buffer size before taking the remainder: (head + size - tail) % size. This gives 0 for an empty buffer, so a completely full buffer cannot be told apart from an empty one and the reader must run often enough to stay behind a full lap.
Incorrect:
size_t availBad(size_t size, size_t head, size_t tail) {
  (void)size;
  return head - tail;
}
Correct:
size_t dmaAvail(size_t size, size_t head, size_t tail) {
  return (head + size - tail) % size;
}
Complexity: O(1)

