Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · dma · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Give DMA the transfer count in items of the configured width, not in bytes
Misconception: The transfer count register is always in bytes.
Explanation: NDTR counts data items of the width configured for the transfer (8, 16 or 32 bits), not bytes. For a 32-bit transfer of 64 bytes the count is 16. Writing 64 makes the controller move four times as much memory and overwrites whatever follows the buffer. Also check that the buffer address is a multiple of the item width.
Incorrect:
uint16_t countBad(size_t bytes, unsigned widthBytes) {
  (void)widthBytes;
  return (uint16_t)bytes;
}
Correct:
uint16_t dmaCount(size_t bytes, unsigned widthBytes) {
  return (uint16_t)(bytes / widthBytes);
}
int dmaAligned(uintptr_t addr, unsigned widthBytes) {
  return addr % widthBytes == 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

