Embedded C · STM32_HAL · dma · mental-model · Intermediate
Concept: Convert the DMA remaining-count register NDTR into the next write index of a circular receive buffer
Misconception: The NDTR register holds the index where DMA will write next.
Explanation: NDTR counts the transfers that are still to be done, and in circular mode it counts down from the buffer size and then reloads. The write position is therefore size - NDTR, and when NDTR has just reloaded to the full size that means index 0. Using NDTR directly as the index mirrors the buffer: the first received byte appears to be at the end.
Incorrect:
size_t headBad(size_t size, size_t ndtr) {
  return ndtr;
}
Correct:
size_t dmaHead(size_t size, size_t ndtr) {
  return (size - ndtr) % size;
}
Complexity: O(1)

