Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · nvic and exti interrupts · mutation · Intermediate
Concept: Acknowledge an EXTI line by writing a 1 to its PR bit with plain assignment
Misconception: EXTI->PR |= bit acknowledges the interrupt.
Explanation: A pending bit in EXTI->PR is cleared by writing 1 to it; writing 0 changes nothing. The read-modify-write form reads PR, ORs in the bit and writes everything back, so every other line that was pending in the copy is written as 1 and is cleared too, even if its handler has not run. Assigning only the bit you handled writes 0 to all the others. If the handler forgets to clear PR at all it runs again immediately.
Incorrect:
void ackBad(unsigned line) {
  EXTI->PR |= 1U << line;
}
Correct:
void extiAck(unsigned line) {
  EXTI->PR = 1U << line;
}
Complexity: O(1)

