Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · serial framing · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Encode with COBS so the packet contains no zero bytes and zero can be the delimiter
Misconception: COBS output can be written in one pass without going back.
Explanation: COBS replaces each zero by a count of the bytes up to the next zero. The encoder reserves a slot for the count, copies non-zero bytes, and when it meets a zero (or has copied 254 bytes) writes the count into the slot and reserves a new one. The final count must be written after the loop, otherwise the last block header is left unset. For {11 22 00 33} the output is 03 11 22 02 33.
Incorrect:
size_t cobsBad(const uint8_t *in, size_t n, uint8_t *out) {
  size_t ci = 0, oi = 1; uint8_t code = 1;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (in[i] == 0) { out[ci] = code; ci = oi++; code = 1; }
    else { out[oi++] = in[i]; if (++code == 0xFF) { out[ci] = code; ci = oi++; code = 1; } }
  }
  return oi;
}
Correct:
size_t cobsEncode(const uint8_t *in, size_t n, uint8_t *out) {
  size_t ci = 0, oi = 1; uint8_t code = 1;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (in[i] == 0) { out[ci] = code; ci = oi++; code = 1; }
    else { out[oi++] = in[i]; if (++code == 0xFF) { out[ci] = code; ci = oi++; code = 1; } }
  }
  out[ci] = code;
  return oi;
}
Complexity: O(n)

