Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · gpio registers · mutation · Intermediate
Concept: Change one output pin atomically by writing BSRR instead of read-modify-write on ODR
Misconception: ODR |= mask is a single safe operation.
Explanation: ODR |= mask is three steps: read ODR, OR, write ODR. If an interrupt changes another pin of the same port between the read and the write, the write puts back the old value and that change is lost. BSRR is write-only: bits 0..15 set pins, bits 16..31 reset pins, and zero bits do nothing, so one store changes exactly the pins you name.
Incorrect:
void pinSetBad(GPIO_TypeDef *g, unsigned pin, void (*mid)(void)) {
  uint32_t v = g->ODR;
  if (mid != NULL) mid();
  g->ODR = v | (1U << pin);
}
Correct:
void pinSet(GPIO_TypeDef *g, unsigned pin) {
  g->BSRR = 1U << pin;
}
void pinClear(GPIO_TypeDef *g, unsigned pin) {
  g->BSRR = 1U << (pin + 16U);
}
Complexity: O(1)

