Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · h-bridge motor driver · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Pass through coast when reversing so the bridge never changes direction in one step
Misconception: The direction can be reversed in a single update.
Explanation: Reversing a spinning motor at once makes it act as a generator and drives a large current back through the bridge and the supply, and with discrete switches it can turn two switches of one leg on together. Go through coast for at least one update (or longer for large motors) before driving the opposite direction.
Incorrect:
int nextBad(int cur, int want) {
  (void)cur;
  return want;
}
Correct:
enum { DIR_COAST = 0, DIR_FWD = 1, DIR_REV = 2 };
int nextDir(int cur, int want) {
  int flip = (cur == DIR_FWD && want == DIR_REV) || (cur == DIR_REV && want == DIR_FWD);
  if (flip) return DIR_COAST;
  return want;
}
Complexity: O(1)

