Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · h-bridge motor driver · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Map speed to duty above the minimum at which the motor starts to turn
Misconception: The duty cycle should be proportional to the speed from zero.
Explanation: A motor does not turn below a minimum duty (stiction), so the low part of a linear map is wasted and the motor just whines. Map the speed range 1..255 onto the usable range from the minimum duty to the maximum, and keep zero as zero.
Incorrect:
int mapBad(int speed, int minDuty, int maxDuty) {
  return speed * maxDuty / 255;
}
Correct:
int mapDuty(int speed, int minDuty, int maxDuty) {
  if (speed <= 0) return 0;
  if (speed > 255) speed = 255;
  return minDuty + (speed - 1) * (maxDuty - minDuty) / 254;
}
Complexity: O(1)

