Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c master · mental-model · Beginner
Concept: Convert a 7-bit I2C address to the left-shifted form the STM32 HAL expects
Misconception: The HAL takes the same 7-bit address that the datasheet prints.
Explanation: Datasheets print a 7-bit I2C address such as 0x48. On the wire the address is followed by the read/write bit, so the first byte is (address << 1) | R/W. The STM32 HAL functions take the address already shifted left by one and set the R/W bit themselves. Passing the raw 7-bit value addresses a different device, so the transfer fails or reaches the wrong chip. Keep the address as 7 bits in your own code and shift it in one helper.
Incorrect:
uint16_t i2cDevBad(uint8_t addr7) {
  return addr7;
}
Correct:
uint16_t i2cDev(uint8_t addr7) {
  return (uint16_t)(addr7 << 1);
}
Complexity: O(1)

