Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · lwip networking · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Send a whole buffer through a socket-style call that may accept only part of it
Misconception: A successful send call has accepted all of the bytes.
Explanation: On a TCP socket, send or lwip_write can return fewer bytes than requested when the send buffer is nearly full. The return value is the number of bytes accepted, and the caller must send the rest. Loop until all bytes are accepted, advance the pointer by the returned count, and treat a result of zero or less as an error so a closed connection cannot make the loop spin forever.
Incorrect:
typedef int (*SendFn)(const uint8_t *, size_t);
int sendBad(SendFn f, const uint8_t *p, size_t n) { return f(p, n); }
Correct:
typedef int (*SendFn)(const uint8_t *, size_t);
int sendAll(SendFn f, const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  size_t done = 0;
  while (done < n) {
    int r = f(p + done, n - done);
    if (r <= 0) return -1;
    done += (size_t)r;
  }
  return (int)done;
}
Complexity: O(n)

