Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · memory mapped io · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Write unlock keys in the order the reference manual gives
Misconception: The two flash unlock keys can be written in any order.
Explanation: Flash and some other registers are protected by a key sequence: write KEY1 (0x45670123) and then KEY2 (0xCDEF89AB) to the key register. A wrong or reversed key typically locks the register until the next reset, and the next write then fails or causes a bus error. Write the keys in manual order and confirm the lock bit before starting an erase or program.
Incorrect:
int unlockBad(void (*wr)(uint32_t)) {
  wr(0xCDEF89ABU);
  wr(0x45670123U);
  return 0;
}
Correct:
int flashUnlock(void (*wr)(uint32_t)) {
  wr(0x45670123U);
  wr(0xCDEF89ABU);
  return 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

