Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · mqtt client · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Build a CONNECT packet for protocol level 4 with the keep-alive in network byte order
Misconception: Multi-byte fields are written in the byte order of the processor.
Explanation: All MQTT 16-bit fields, such as the keep-alive and every string length, are big-endian. A CONNECT packet is the byte 0x10, the remaining length, the protocol name "MQTT" with its length 00 04, the level 04, the flags (02 for a clean session), the keep-alive and then the length-prefixed client identifier. Client "a1" with a 60 second keep-alive gives 10 0E 00 04 4D 51 54 54 04 02 00 3C 00 02 61 31. Writing the keep-alive low byte first on a little-endian MCU turns 60 seconds into 15360 seconds.
Incorrect:
int mqConnectBad(uint8_t *o, const char *id, uint16_t keep) {
  size_t il = strlen(id);
  int n = 0;
  static const uint8_t hdr[] = {0x00, 0x04, 'M', 'Q', 'T', 'T', 0x04, 0x02};
  o[n++] = 0x10;
  n += mqEncLen((uint32_t)(12 + il), o + n);
  memcpy(o + n, hdr, 8); n += 8;
  memcpy(o + n, &keep, 2); n += 2;
  o[n++] = (uint8_t)(il >> 8); o[n++] = (uint8_t)(il & 0xFFU);
  memcpy(o + n, id, il); n += (int)il;
  return n;
}
Correct:
int mqConnect(uint8_t *o, const char *id, uint16_t keep) {
  size_t il = strlen(id);
  int n = 0;
  static const uint8_t hdr[] = {0x00, 0x04, 'M', 'Q', 'T', 'T', 0x04, 0x02};
  o[n++] = 0x10;
  n += mqEncLen((uint32_t)(12 + il), o + n);
  memcpy(o + n, hdr, 8); n += 8;
  o[n++] = (uint8_t)(keep >> 8); o[n++] = (uint8_t)(keep & 0xFFU);
  o[n++] = (uint8_t)(il >> 8); o[n++] = (uint8_t)(il & 0xFFU);
  memcpy(o + n, id, il); n += (int)il;
  return n;
}
Complexity: O(n)

