Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · oled display over spi · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Find the pages that changed by comparing the whole page, not only its first byte
Misconception: Sending only the changed pages saves SPI time, and the first byte of a page is enough to tell if it changed.
Explanation: A full frame is 1024 bytes, which takes about a millisecond at 10 MHz, but it is wasted time when only a small area changes. Compare the old and new content page by page (128 bytes each) and build a bit mask of changed pages. Comparing only the first byte of each page misses changes elsewhere in the page.
Incorrect:
unsigned dirtyBad(const uint8_t *a, const uint8_t *b) {
  unsigned m = 0;
  for (int p = 0; p < 8; p++) if (a[p * 128] != b[p * 128]) m |= 1U << p;
  return m;
}
Correct:
unsigned dirtyPages(const uint8_t *a, const uint8_t *b) {
  unsigned m = 0;
  for (int p = 0; p < 8; p++) if (memcmp(a + p * 128, b + p * 128, 128) != 0) m |= 1U << p;
  return m;
}
Complexity: O(n)

