Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · oled display over spi · mental-model · Intermediate
Concept: Address a pixel in the page-organised SSD1306 frame buffer
Misconception: The frame buffer stores the pixels row by row, eight pixels to a byte along each row.
Explanation: An SSD1306 128 x 64 display is organised in 8 pages of 8 rows. Each byte is a vertical strip of 8 pixels: the byte index is x + (y / 8) x 128 and the bit is y % 8. A row-major packing, with eight horizontal pixels per byte, puts the bits in the wrong places on the screen. Check the bounds before writing so a stray coordinate cannot overwrite memory.
Incorrect:
void pixBad(uint8_t *buf, int x, int y) {
  buf[(y * 128 + x) / 8] |= (uint8_t)(1U << (x % 8));
}
Correct:
void setPixel(uint8_t *buf, int x, int y, int on) {
  if (x < 0 || x >= 128 || y < 0 || y >= 64) return;
  uint8_t m = (uint8_t)(1U << (y % 8));
  if (on) buf[x + (y / 8) * 128] |= m;
  else buf[x + (y / 8) * 128] &= (uint8_t)~m;
}
Complexity: O(1)

