Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · oled display over spi · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Draw a 5 by 7 glyph with a blank column and clip it at the right edge of the buffer
Misconception: A glyph can be copied to the buffer at any column.
Explanation: A 5-column glyph takes six columns with one blank column for spacing. Near the right edge the copy must stop at column 127; without the check the write continues into the next page, or beyond the end of the buffer in the last page, and corrupts memory. Return the next free column so a string can be drawn one glyph after another.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: stack-buffer-overflow):
int glyphBad(uint8_t *buf, int x, int page, const uint8_t *g) {
  for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) buf[page * 128 + x + i] = g[i];
  return x + 6;
}
Correct:
int drawGlyph(uint8_t *buf, int x, int page, const uint8_t *g) {
  for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
    if (x + i >= 128) break;
    buf[page * 128 + x + i] = i < 5 ? g[i] : 0;
  }
  return x + 6;
}
Complexity: O(1)

