Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pointers · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Read values from a buffer through a pointer-to-pointer cursor that the callee advances
Misconception: Incrementing a pointer parameter moves the caller cursor as well.
Explanation: C passes pointers by value, so a function that increments its own copy of a pointer leaves the caller cursor where it was. To let the callee advance the cursor, pass the address of the pointer (a pointer to pointer) and bound the read by an end pointer.
Incorrect:
int getBad(const uint8_t *cur, const uint8_t *end, uint8_t *out) {
  if (cur >= end) return -1;
  *out = *cur++;
  return 0;
}
Correct:
int getU8(const uint8_t **cur, const uint8_t *end, uint8_t *out) {
  if (*cur >= end) return -1;
  *out = *(*cur)++;
  return 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

