Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pointers · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Dispatch through a table of function pointers after checking the index and the entry
Misconception: A table of handlers can be called directly with any index.
Explanation: Callbacks and command tables are arrays of function pointers. Check the index against the table size and the entry against NULL before calling, because calling a NULL function pointer jumps to address 0. Declare the pointer type with a typedef so the signature is stated once.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: SEGV):
typedef int (*Handler)(int);
int dispatchBad(Handler *t, size_t n, size_t i, int arg) {
  (void)n;
  return t[i](arg);
}
Correct:
typedef int (*Handler)(int);
int dispatch(Handler *t, size_t n, size_t i, int arg) {
  if (i >= n || t[i] == NULL) return -1;
  return t[i](arg);
}
Complexity: O(1)

