Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pointers · mental-model · Intermediate
Concept: Pass the element count with an array because a function parameter is only a pointer
Misconception: sizeof on an array parameter gives the size of the array.
Explanation: An array passed to a function decays to a pointer to its first element, so inside the function sizeof gives the size of a pointer: 4 bytes on a Cortex-M or Xtensa core, 2 on AVR, 8 on a 64-bit host. The function cannot know the length. Pass the length as a separate parameter and compute it at the call site with sizeof array / sizeof array[0].
Incorrect:
size_t lenBad(const uint8_t *p) {
  return sizeof p;
}
Correct:
#define COUNT_OF(a) (sizeof(a) / sizeof((a)[0]))
uint32_t sumBytes(const uint8_t *p, size_t n) {
  uint32_t s = 0;
  while (n--) s += *p++;
  return s;
}
Complexity: O(1)

