Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pwm timers · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Start PWM on channel 1 with preload enabled and an update event to load the prescaler
Misconception: Writing PSC, ARR and CCR1 and setting CEN is all that is needed.
Explanation: The channel needs mode 110 (PWM mode 1) in OC1M, output compare preload OC1PE so CCR1 changes only at a period boundary, and CC1E in CCER to connect the output. PSC and ARR are buffered; an update event (EGR.UG) loads them immediately instead of after the first period. The pin itself must be set to the alternate function for that timer.
Incorrect:
void pwmStartBad(TIM_TypeDef *t, uint32_t psc, uint32_t arr, uint32_t ccr) {
  t->PSC = psc;
  t->ARR = arr;
  t->CCR1 = ccr;
  t->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
Correct:
void pwmStartCh1(TIM_TypeDef *t, uint32_t psc, uint32_t arr, uint32_t ccr) {
  t->PSC = psc;
  t->ARR = arr;
  t->CCR1 = ccr;
  t->CCMR1 = TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_2 | TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_1 | TIM_CCMR1_OC1PE;
  t->CCER |= TIM_CCER_CC1E;
  t->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_ARPE;
  t->EGR = TIM_EGR_UG;
  t->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
Complexity: O(1)

