Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pwm timers · transformation · Beginner
Concept: Set the compare value to (ARR + 1) * duty / 100 so 100 percent really is always on
Misconception: CCR = ARR * duty / 100.
Explanation: In PWM mode 1 the output is high while the counter is below CCR, and the counter takes ARR + 1 values. A compare value of ARR + 1 keeps the output high for the whole period; ARR leaves one low tick at 100 percent. Scale with ARR + 1 and multiply before dividing so integer division does not lose the fraction. CCR = 0 gives a constantly low output.
Incorrect:
uint32_t ccrBad(uint32_t arr, uint32_t pct) {
  return arr * pct / 100U;
}
Correct:
uint32_t pwmCcr(uint32_t arr, uint32_t pct) {
  return (arr + 1U) * pct / 100U;
}
Complexity: O(1)

