Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · pwm timers · transformation · Beginner
Concept: Compute the auto-reload value as timer clock / ((PSC + 1) * frequency) - 1
Misconception: The period register ARR equals timer clock divided by (prescaler times frequency).
Explanation: The counter runs at clock / (PSC + 1) and counts 0 to ARR, which is ARR + 1 steps per period. So frequency = clock / ((PSC + 1) * (ARR + 1)) and ARR = clock / ((PSC + 1) * frequency) - 1. Both registers hold the value minus one: PSC = 0 divides by one and ARR = 0 gives one step. Forgetting the minus one makes every period one tick too long.
Incorrect:
uint32_t arrBad(uint32_t clk, uint32_t psc, uint32_t hz) {
  return clk / ((psc + 1U) * hz);
}
Correct:
uint32_t pwmArr(uint32_t clk, uint32_t psc, uint32_t hz) {
  return clk / ((psc + 1U) * hz) - 1U;
}
Complexity: O(1)

