Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · reset and brown-out · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Decode the reset cause from RCC CSR by testing the specific causes before the pin reset flag
Misconception: The first reset flag found in CSR is the cause of the reset.
Explanation: On STM32F4 the pin-reset flag is set by every reset that comes through the reset line, including a power-on reset, a brown-out reset and a watchdog reset, and the brown-out flag is set by a power-on as well. Test the specific causes first (independent watchdog, window watchdog, low-power, software, power-on), then brown-out, and report pin reset only when nothing else is set.
Incorrect:
int causeBad(uint32_t csr) {
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_PINRSTF) return 1;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_IWDGRSTF) return 2;
  return 0;
}
Correct:
enum { RC_UNKNOWN, RC_PIN, RC_IWDG, RC_WWDG, RC_LPWR, RC_SOFT, RC_POR, RC_BOR };
int resetCause(uint32_t csr) {
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_IWDGRSTF) return RC_IWDG;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_WWDGRSTF) return RC_WWDG;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_LPWRRSTF) return RC_LPWR;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_SFTRSTF) return RC_SOFT;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_PORRSTF) return RC_POR;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_BORRSTF) return RC_BOR;
  if (csr & RCC_CSR_PINRSTF) return RC_PIN;
  return RC_UNKNOWN;
}
Complexity: O(1)

