Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · reset and brown-out · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Add hysteresis to a software low-voltage alarm so it does not chatter at the threshold
Misconception: A single threshold is enough to decide whether the supply is low.
Explanation: The measured supply voltage has noise, so with one threshold the alarm toggles every time the reading wobbles around it. Use two thresholds: enter the low state below the low threshold and leave it only above a higher threshold. In between, keep the previous state.
Incorrect:
int lowBad(int mv, int state, int lowMv, int highMv) {
  (void)state; (void)highMv;
  return mv < lowMv;
}
Correct:
int lowState(int mv, int state, int lowMv, int highMv) {
  if (mv < lowMv) return 1;
  if (mv > highMv) return 0;
  return state;
}
Complexity: O(1)

