Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos semaphores and mutexes · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Release a mutex on every return path of the function that took it
Misconception: A function can return as soon as it hits an error while holding the mutex.
Explanation: A mutex taken at the start of a function stays locked until some task gives it back. An early return on an error path that skips the give leaves the mutex locked for good, and the next task that takes it blocks forever. Take the mutex, do the work in one block, give once at a single exit point.
Incorrect:
int updateBad(SemaphoreHandle_t m, int fail) {
  if (xSemaphoreTake(m, 0) != pdTRUE) return -1;
  if (fail) return -2;
  xSemaphoreGive(m);
  return 0;
}
Correct:
int updateOk(SemaphoreHandle_t m, int fail) {
  int rc = 0;
  if (xSemaphoreTake(m, 0) != pdTRUE) return -1;
  if (fail) rc = -2;
  xSemaphoreGive(m);
  return rc;
}
Complexity: O(1)

