Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos semaphores and mutexes · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Treat a failed xSemaphoreGive as a bug when a counting semaphore guards a pool of slots
Misconception: Giving a semaphore always succeeds.
Explanation: A counting semaphore created with a maximum count refuses a give that would exceed it and returns pdFALSE. When it guards a pool of slots, a refused give means a slot was released twice. Check the result, count the errors and treat them as a defect.
Incorrect:
void releaseBad(SemaphoreHandle_t s) {
  xSemaphoreGive(s);
}
Correct:
int releaseSlot(SemaphoreHandle_t s) {
  return xSemaphoreGive(s) == pdTRUE ? 0 : -1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

