Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos tasks · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Convert milliseconds to ticks and never pass zero ticks to vTaskDelay
Misconception: vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(ms)) delays for ms milliseconds for any ms.
Explanation: The tick rate in ESP-IDF defaults to 100 Hz, so one tick is 10 ms and pdMS_TO_TICKS(5) is 0. vTaskDelay(0) does not block, so a loop that thinks it sleeps 5 ms actually spins and starves lower-priority tasks and the idle task (which feeds the task watchdog). Round up and use at least one tick.
Incorrect:
void delayBad(uint32_t ms) {
  vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(ms));
}
Correct:
void delayMs(uint32_t ms) {
  TickType_t t = pdMS_TO_TICKS(ms);
  if (t == 0) t = 1;
  vTaskDelay(t);
}
Complexity: O(1)

