Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos tasks · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Run a periodic task with vTaskDelayUntil so the work time does not stretch the period
Misconception: Calling vTaskDelay with the period after the work keeps a fixed rate.
Explanation: vTaskDelay waits a time counted from the call, so the loop period is the work time plus the delay. vTaskDelayUntil waits until a point counted from the previous wake-up time, so the period stays fixed as long as the work is shorter than the period. Initialise the wake time once with xTaskGetTickCount before the loop.
Incorrect:
TickType_t periodBad(int n, TickType_t work, TickType_t period) {
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { hw_ticks += work; vTaskDelay(period); }
  return xTaskGetTickCount();
}
Correct:
TickType_t periodGood(int n, TickType_t work, TickType_t period) {
  TickType_t last = xTaskGetTickCount();
  for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { hw_ticks += work; vTaskDelayUntil(&last, period); }
  return xTaskGetTickCount();
}
Complexity: O(n)

