Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · rtos tasks · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Compute the stack actually used from the high-water mark, which reports the smallest free space
Misconception: uxTaskGetStackHighWaterMark returns how much stack the task has used.
Explanation: The high-water mark is the minimum amount of stack that has ever been free, not the amount used. Used stack is the total minus the high-water mark. A task with 2048 bytes total and a high-water mark of 300 has used 1748 bytes and is close to overflow; reading 300 as the usage would suggest a large margin.
Incorrect:
uint32_t usedBad(uint32_t total, uint32_t highWater) {
  (void)total;
  return highWater;
}
Correct:
uint32_t stackUsed(uint32_t total, uint32_t highWater) {
  return total - highWater;
}
int stackLow(uint32_t total, uint32_t highWater, uint32_t margin) {
  return highWater < margin && total > 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

