Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · static allocation · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Allocate from a bump arena and round each offset up to the requested alignment
Misconception: A bump arena can hand out the next free byte.
Explanation: A bump arena moves an offset forward on every allocation and is released all at once by resetting the offset. The next free byte may not be suitably aligned: a uint32_t needs an address that is a multiple of 4, and a misaligned access faults on Cortex-M0. Round the offset up with (off + align - 1) & ~(align - 1) before handing out the block, and fail when the arena is exhausted.
Incorrect:
typedef struct { uint8_t mem[64]; size_t off; } Arena;
void *arenaBad(Arena *a, size_t n, size_t align) {
  (void)align;
  if (a->off + n > sizeof a->mem) return NULL;
  void *p = a->mem + a->off;
  a->off += n;
  return p;
}
Correct:
typedef struct { uint8_t mem[64]; size_t off; } Arena;
void *arenaAlloc(Arena *a, size_t n, size_t align) {
  size_t o = (a->off + align - 1U) & ~(align - 1U);
  if (o + n > sizeof a->mem) return NULL;
  a->off = o + n;
  return a->mem + o;
}
void arenaReset(Arena *a) { a->off = 0; }
Complexity: O(1)

