Embedded C · STM32_HAL · superloop and scheduler · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Test whether a task is due with unsigned subtraction so the 32-bit tick counter can wrap
Misconception: A task is due when the tick counter has reached last plus the period.
Explanation: A free-running 32-bit millisecond counter wraps after about 49.7 days. The test now >= last + period fails near the wrap: the sum wraps to a small number and the task looks due immediately, or the counter wraps and the comparison never succeeds. The difference (uint32_t)(now - last) is correct across the wrap as long as the period is shorter than half the counter range.
Incorrect:
int dueBad(uint32_t now, uint32_t last, uint32_t period) {
  return now >= last + period;
}
Correct:
int due(uint32_t now, uint32_t last, uint32_t period) {
  return (uint32_t)(now - last) >= period;
}
Complexity: O(1)

