Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · superloop and scheduler · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Convert milliseconds to ticks rounding up so a delay is never shorter than requested
Misconception: Dividing milliseconds by the tick period in integer arithmetic gives the right tick count.
Explanation: With a 100 Hz tick one tick is 10 ms. Truncating 5 ms gives 0 ticks, so the delay does not happen at all, and 15 ms gives 1 tick, which is 10 ms. Round up: (ms x hz + 999) / 1000. Multiply in 64 bits, because ms x hz can exceed 32 bits.
Incorrect:
uint32_t ticksBad(uint32_t ms, uint32_t hz) {
  return ms * hz / 1000U;
}
Correct:
uint32_t msToTicks(uint32_t ms, uint32_t hz) {
  return (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)ms * hz + 999U) / 1000U);
}
Complexity: O(1)

