Embedded C · STM32_HAL · stack and heap · creation · Intermediate
Concept: Check the multiplication of count and element size before allocating an array
Misconception: malloc(n * size) allocates the array whatever the values of n and size.
Explanation: On a 32-bit microcontroller size_t is 32 bits, so n * size can wrap around to a small number. malloc then succeeds with a small block and the code that writes n elements overruns it. Divide the limit by the element size before allocating, and reject zero sizes.
Incorrect:
void *allocBad(size_t n, size_t size) {
  return malloc(n * size);
}
Correct:
void *allocArray(size_t n, size_t size) {
  if (size == 0 || n > SIZE_MAX / size) return NULL;
  return malloc(n * size);
}
Complexity: O(1)

