Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · sleep modes · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Compute the RTC wake-up timer reload for a wake interval, which counts from the value to zero
Misconception: The wake-up timer reload value equals the number of clock ticks in the interval.
Explanation: The RTC wake-up timer counts down from the reload value to zero and fires on the underflow, so it runs for reload + 1 ticks. For an interval of N ticks write N - 1. With the 32768 Hz LSE divided by 16 (2048 Hz) a 1 second interval is 2048 ticks and the reload is 2047. The reload is 16 bits wide, so intervals longer than 65536 ticks need a different clock selection.
Incorrect:
int wutBad(uint32_t ms, uint32_t hz) {
  return (int)((uint64_t)ms * hz / 1000U);
}
Correct:
int wutReload(uint32_t ms, uint32_t hz) {
  uint64_t ticks = (uint64_t)ms * hz / 1000U;
  if (ticks == 0 || ticks - 1 > 0xFFFFU) return -1;
  return (int)(ticks - 1);
}
Complexity: O(1)

