Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c sensor drivers · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Read the six acceleration bytes in one burst and combine each pair as big-endian signed values
Misconception: The low byte of each axis comes first.
Explanation: MPU-6050 style devices store each axis as a signed 16-bit value with the high byte at the lower register address. Reading all six bytes in one transaction gives a consistent x, y, z snapshot (the registers are latched during a burst); reading them one by one can mix values from different samples. Combine each pair as (high << 8) | low and convert to int16_t.
Incorrect:
int accelBad(I2C_HandleTypeDef *h, uint8_t a7, int16_t *xyz) {
  uint8_t b[6];
  if (HAL_I2C_Mem_Read(h, (uint16_t)(a7 << 1), 0x3B,
                       I2C_MEMADD_SIZE_8BIT, b, 6, 10) != HAL_OK) return -1;
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) xyz[i] = (int16_t)(((uint16_t)b[2 * i + 1] << 8) | b[2 * i]);
  return 0;
}
Correct:
int accelRead(I2C_HandleTypeDef *h, uint8_t a7, int16_t *xyz) {
  uint8_t b[6];
  if (HAL_I2C_Mem_Read(h, (uint16_t)(a7 << 1), 0x3B,
                       I2C_MEMADD_SIZE_8BIT, b, 6, 10) != HAL_OK) return -1;
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) xyz[i] = (int16_t)(((uint16_t)b[2 * i] << 8) | b[2 * i + 1]);
  return 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

