Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c sensor drivers · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Reject single-sample spikes by taking the median of three readings
Misconception: The average of three readings removes a spike.
Explanation: A single bad reading, such as a bit error on the bus, shifts a mean of three by a third of its size. The median of three ignores one outlier completely: sort the three values and take the middle one. It needs only comparisons and no division.
Incorrect:
int med3Bad(int a, int b, int c) {
  return (a + b + c) / 3;
}
Correct:
int med3(int a, int b, int c) {
  if (a > b) { int t = a; a = b; b = t; }
  if (b > c) { int t = b; b = c; c = t; }
