Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · i2c sensor drivers · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Convert a 12-bit left-justified two-complement temperature into millidegrees
Misconception: The two result bytes can be combined and shifted right by four to get the temperature.
Explanation: A TMP102-style sensor returns two bytes with the 12-bit result in the upper bits, 0.0625 degrees per step, in two-complement. Shifting the unsigned 16-bit value right by four loses the sign: 0xE700 (a negative temperature) becomes 3696. Extend the sign of the 12-bit value and then multiply by 625 and divide by 10 for millidegrees.
Incorrect:
int tmpBad(uint8_t hi, uint8_t lo) {
  int raw = ((hi << 8) | lo) >> 4;
  return raw * 625 / 10;
}
Correct:
int tmpMilliC(uint8_t hi, uint8_t lo) {
  int raw = ((hi << 8) | lo) >> 4;
  if (raw & 0x800) raw -= 4096;
  return raw * 625 / 10;
}
Complexity: O(1)

