Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · spi master · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Pick the smallest divider code BR whose clock stays at or below the device maximum
Misconception: The SPI clock is the peripheral clock shifted right by BR.
Explanation: The 3-bit field BR selects a divider of 2^(BR + 1): code 0 divides by 2 and code 7 by 256. The clock is pclk >> (BR + 1). Leaving out the plus one makes the code appear to be one step faster than it really is, so the search stops one step too late and the bus runs slower than needed. Choose the smallest code (fastest clock) that does not exceed the slave maximum.
Incorrect:
unsigned brBad(uint32_t pclk, uint32_t maxHz) {
  for (unsigned br = 0; br < 8; br++)
    if ((pclk >> br) <= maxHz) return br;
  return 7;
}
Correct:
unsigned spiBr(uint32_t pclk, uint32_t maxHz) {
  for (unsigned br = 0; br < 8; br++)
    if ((pclk >> (br + 1U)) <= maxHz) return br;
  return 7;
}
Complexity: O(1)

