Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · spi master · mental-model · Beginner
Concept: Map SPI mode 0 to 3 to clock polarity (CPOL, high bit) and clock phase (CPHA, low bit)
Misconception: The mode number is CPHA in the high bit and CPOL in the low bit.
Explanation: SPI mode n is the two-bit number CPOL CPHA: CPOL is the idle level of the clock and CPHA says whether data is sampled on the first (leading) clock edge or the second. Mode 0 is CPOL 0 CPHA 0, mode 1 is CPOL 0 CPHA 1, mode 2 is CPOL 1 CPHA 0 and mode 3 is CPOL 1 CPHA 1. Swapping the two bits makes modes 1 and 2 trade places, and the device returns shifted garbage. The datasheet of the slave names the mode it needs.
Incorrect:
void modeBad(int mode, int *cpol, int *cpha) {
  *cpol = mode & 1;
  *cpha = (mode >> 1) & 1;
}
Correct:
void spiMode(int mode, int *cpol, int *cpha) {
  *cpol = (mode >> 1) & 1;
  *cpha = mode & 1;
}
Complexity: O(1)

