Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · structs and unions · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Serialise a multi-byte field into a wire buffer byte by byte instead of casting a pointer
Misconception: Casting a byte buffer pointer to uint16_t * is fine if the data is at the right place.
Explanation: A byte buffer can start at any address, and a field at an odd offset is not aligned for a 16-bit or 32-bit access. Dereferencing a misaligned pointer is undefined behaviour in C and faults or traps on some cores such as the Cortex-M0. Build and read the field with shifts and masks, or copy it with memcpy; the result is also independent of how the structure is padded.
Incorrect (undefined behaviour reported by the sanitizer: misaligned):
uint16_t rd16Bad(const uint8_t *p) {
  return *(const uint16_t *)p;
}
Correct:
uint16_t rd16(const uint8_t *p) {
  return (uint16_t)(p[0] | (p[1] << 8));
}
void wr16(uint8_t *p, uint16_t v) {
  p[0] = (uint8_t)v;
  p[1] = (uint8_t)(v >> 8);
}
Complexity: O(1)

