Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · servo and stepper motors · iteration · Intermediate
Concept: Step a four-phase stepper through an eight-entry half-step table in either direction
Misconception: The phase index can be advanced with the remainder operator for both directions.
Explanation: Half-stepping energises the coils in an eight-entry pattern, and the index advances by +1 for one direction and -1 for the other. In C the remainder of a negative number is negative, so (phase + dir) % 8 gives -1 when stepping back from phase 0 and indexes outside the table. Add the table size before taking the remainder, or mask with 7.
Incorrect:
int phaseBad(int phase, int dir) {
  return (phase + dir) % 8;
}
Correct:
static const uint8_t halfStep[8] = {0x1, 0x3, 0x2, 0x6, 0x4, 0xC, 0x8, 0x9};
int stepPhase(int phase, int dir) {
  return (phase + 8 + dir) & 7;
}
uint8_t coils(int phase) { return halfStep[phase & 7]; }
Complexity: O(1)

