Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · structs and unions · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Read the bit pattern of a float through a union instead of converting the value
Misconception: Casting a float to uint32_t gives the bit pattern of the float.
Explanation: A cast converts the value: 1.0f becomes 1. To see the stored bits, write the float into one member of a union and read the uint32_t member; C11 defines this. The bits of 1.0f are 0x3F800000. Pointer casts such as *(uint32_t *)&f break the aliasing rules and can be miscompiled when optimisation is on.
Incorrect:
uint32_t floatBitsBad(float f) {
  return (uint32_t)f;
}
Correct:
uint32_t floatBits(float f) {
  union { float f; uint32_t u; } x;
  x.f = f;
  return x.u;
}
Complexity: O(1)

