Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · servo and stepper motors · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Clamp the servo command to the mechanical limits at both ends
Misconception: Clamping the upper limit is enough to protect a servo.
Explanation: Driving a servo beyond the travel of its linkage makes it stall against the stop, draw high current and overheat. Clamp the command to both the lower and the upper limit of the mechanism, not only the upper one.
Incorrect:
int clampBad(int a, int lo, int hi) {
  (void)lo;
  return a > hi ? hi : a;
}
Correct:
int clampAngle(int a, int lo, int hi) {
  if (a < lo) return lo;
  if (a > hi) return hi;
  return a;
}
Complexity: O(1)

