Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · hardware timers · mutation · Intermediate
Concept: Clear a write-0-to-clear status flag by assigning its complement, not by read-modify-write
Misconception: SR &= ~UIF clears only the update flag.
Explanation: Status bits such as UIF are cleared by writing 0 to them, and writing 1 leaves them unchanged. The read-modify-write form reads SR, clears one bit in the copy and writes the copy back; any other flag that was set after the read is written back as 0 and is cleared without ever being seen. Assigning ~UIF writes 1 to every other bit, which leaves them alone.
Incorrect:
void clearBad(TIM_TypeDef *t, void (*mid)(void)) {
  uint32_t v = t->SR;
  if (mid != NULL) mid();
  t->SR = v & ~TIM_SR_UIF;
}
Correct:
volatile uint32_t ticks1ms;
void TIM2_IRQHandler(void) {
  if (TIM2->SR & TIM_SR_UIF) {
    TIM2->SR = ~TIM_SR_UIF;
    ticks1ms++;
  }
}
void clearFlag(TIM_TypeDef *t) {
  t->SR = ~TIM_SR_UIF;
}
Complexity: O(1)

