Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · hardware timers · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Measure elapsed counts with unsigned subtraction in the counter width so wraparound cancels out
Misconception: If now is smaller than start the counter has not moved, so the elapsed time is 0.
Explanation: A free-running 16-bit counter wraps from 65535 to 0. Unsigned subtraction wraps the same way, so (uint16_t)(now - start) is the correct number of ticks even when now < start, provided the real interval is shorter than one full period. Testing now > start discards every measurement that crosses the wrap.
Incorrect:
uint16_t elapsedBad(uint16_t now, uint16_t start) {
  return now > start ? (uint16_t)(now - start) : 0;
}
Correct:
uint16_t elapsed16(uint16_t now, uint16_t start) {
  return (uint16_t)(now - start);
}
Complexity: O(1)

