Context: platform: STM32_HAL
Embedded C · STM32_HAL · watchdog timers · edge-cases · Intermediate
Concept: Refresh a window watchdog only while its counter is inside the allowed window
Misconception: A window watchdog can be refreshed at any time before it runs out.
Explanation: The window watchdog (WWDG) counts down a 7-bit counter and resets the chip when it falls below 0x40. It also resets the chip if it is refreshed too early: the refresh is valid only while the counter is at or below the window value W and still at least 0x40. A loop that runs too fast or too slow both fail, which catches runaway code that an independent watchdog would not.
Incorrect:
int canRefreshBad(uint8_t counter, uint8_t window) {
  (void)window;
  return counter >= 0x40;
}
Correct:
int wwdgCanRefresh(uint8_t counter, uint8_t window) {
  return counter >= 0x40 && counter <= window;
}
Complexity: O(1)

