Context: platform: ESP_IDF
Embedded C · ESP_IDF · wifi station · patterns · Intermediate
Concept: Drive the station connection with a state machine that resets the retry count when an address is obtained
Misconception: The retry counter counts all disconnects since boot.
Explanation: The station keeps a state and a retry counter that the event handler updates. A disconnect while the counter is below the limit increments it and goes back to connecting; at the limit the state becomes failed. Obtaining an IP address must reset the counter, otherwise disconnects spread over days add up and a healthy device eventually gives up on the first brief outage.
Incorrect:
typedef enum { WF_IDLE, WF_CONNECTING, WF_CONNECTED, WF_FAILED } WfState;
typedef enum { EV_START, EV_GOT_IP, EV_DISCONNECTED } WfEvent;
typedef struct { WfState st; int retries; } Wf;
void wfStepBad(Wf *w, WfEvent e, int maxRetry) {
  switch (e) {
    case EV_START: w->st = WF_CONNECTING; w->retries = 0; break;
    case EV_GOT_IP: w->st = WF_CONNECTED; break;
    case EV_DISCONNECTED:
      if (w->retries < maxRetry) { w->retries++; w->st = WF_CONNECTING; }
      else w->st = WF_FAILED;
      break;
  }
}
Correct:
typedef enum { WF_IDLE, WF_CONNECTING, WF_CONNECTED, WF_FAILED } WfState;
typedef enum { EV_START, EV_GOT_IP, EV_DISCONNECTED } WfEvent;
typedef struct { WfState st; int retries; } Wf;
void wfStep(Wf *w, WfEvent e, int maxRetry) {
  switch (e) {
    case EV_START: w->st = WF_CONNECTING; w->retries = 0; break;
    case EV_GOT_IP: w->st = WF_CONNECTED; w->retries = 0; break;
    case EV_DISCONNECTED:
      if (w->retries < maxRetry) { w->retries++; w->st = WF_CONNECTING; }
      else w->st = WF_FAILED;
      break;
  }
}
Complexity: O(1)

