Embedded C · STM32_HAL · ws2812 led strips · mental-model · Beginner
Concept: Pack a colour in green, red, blue order with the most significant bit sent first
Misconception: The WS2812 takes its colour bytes in red, green, blue order.
Explanation: A WS2812 expects 24 bits per LED in the order green, red, blue, each byte sent most significant bit first. Packing red first swaps the red and green channels, so red shows as green. The same order applies to the SK6812 and most compatible parts; RGBW parts add a white byte.
Incorrect:
uint32_t packBad(uint8_t r, uint8_t g, uint8_t b) {
  return ((uint32_t)r << 16) | ((uint32_t)g << 8) | b;
}
Correct:
uint32_t packGrb(uint8_t r, uint8_t g, uint8_t b) {
  return ((uint32_t)g << 16) | ((uint32_t)r << 8) | b;
}
Complexity: O(1)

