Embedded C · STM32_HAL · ws2812 led strips · transformation · Intermediate
Concept: Scale a channel by a brightness of 0 to 255 so that full brightness leaves the value unchanged
Misconception: Multiplying by the brightness and shifting right by eight scales a channel.
Explanation: Dividing by 256 instead of 255 makes the largest result one step too small: 255 x 255 >> 8 is 254, so full brightness never reaches full value. Divide by 255 with rounding: (value x brightness + 127) / 255.
Incorrect:
uint8_t scaleBad(uint8_t v, uint8_t br) {
  return (uint8_t)((v * br) >> 8);
}
Correct:
uint8_t scale8(uint8_t v, uint8_t br) {
  return (uint8_t)((v * br + 127) / 255);
}
Complexity: O(1)

