Python (embedded) · serial framing, checksums and CRCs · equality · L2
Concept: The same polynomial with a different start value is a different CRC-16
Misconception: Any CRC-16 with polynomial 0x1021 is CRC-CCITT.
Explanation: The polynomial 0x1021 is shared by several algorithms. CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE starts at 0xFFFF and gives 0x29B1 for b"123456789"; starting at 0x0000 gives the XMODEM variant, 0x31C3. Both ends must agree on initial value, polynomial, bit order and final xor, so write the parameters into the protocol description.
Incorrect:
def crc16_xmodem(data):
    crc = 0x0000
    for b in data:
        crc ^= b << 8
        for _ in range(8):
            crc = ((crc << 1) ^ 0x1021) & 0xFFFF if crc & 0x8000 else (crc << 1) & 0xFFFF
    return crc
Correct:
def crc16_ccitt(data, init=0xFFFF):
    crc = init
    for b in data:
        crc ^= b << 8
        for _ in range(8):
            if crc & 0x8000:
                crc = ((crc << 1) ^ 0x1021) & 0xFFFF
            else:
                crc = (crc << 1) & 0xFFFF
    return crc
Complexity: O(8n)

