Python (embedded) · serial framing, checksums and CRCs · edge-cases · L3
Concept: Escape the end marker inside the payload with byte stuffing
Misconception: A payload can contain any byte without special treatment.
Explanation: If a frame ends at byte 0xC0, a payload that contains 0xC0 ends it early. SLIP replaces 0xC0 inside the data with 0xDB 0xDC and 0xDB with 0xDB 0xDD. Escape 0xDB first or the escape bytes are escaped twice, and decode by reversing the pairs.
Incorrect:
def slip_bad(data):
    return bytes(data) + b"\xc0"
Correct:
def slip(data):
    out = bytearray()
    for b in data:
        if b == 0xC0:
            out.extend(b"\xdb\xdc")
        elif b == 0xDB:
            out.extend(b"\xdb\xdd")
        else:
            out.append(b)
    out.append(0xC0)
    return bytes(out)
def unslip(frame):
    out = bytearray()
    i = 0
    while i < len(frame) and frame[i] != 0xC0:
        if frame[i] == 0xDB:
            i += 1
            out.append(0xC0 if frame[i] == 0xDC else 0xDB)
        else:
            out.append(frame[i])
        i += 1
    return bytes(out)
Complexity: O(n)

