Python (embedded) · a tick-based cooperative scheduler · patterns · L3
Concept: Catch exceptions per task so one faulty task does not stop the others
Misconception: An exception in one task is fine; the scheduler restarts.
Explanation: If the scheduler loop does not catch an exception, a bug in one rarely used task ends the whole loop and every task stops. Wrap each call in try and except Exception, record the error, and keep going. Count failures so a repeatedly failing task can be disabled.
Incorrect:
