Python · sorting · fit-and-alternatives · L2
Concept: Use the built-in sort: Timsort is O(n) on already-sorted runs and O(n log n) otherwise, far ahead of hand-written O(n^2) sorts
Misconception: A simple bubble sort is good enough because the list is nearly sorted.
Explanation: Timsort finds runs that are already ordered and merges them, so sorted input costs n - 1 comparisons and random input about n log n. A bubble sort without an early exit always makes n(n - 1)/2 comparisons. Write your own sort only to learn the algorithm or when the built-in does not fit the problem, for example counting sort on a small integer range.
Incorrect:
def bubble_sort_bad(a):
    a = list(a)
    for i in range(len(a)):
        for j in range(len(a) - 1 - i):
            if a[j + 1] < a[j]:
                a[j], a[j + 1] = a[j + 1], a[j]
    return a
Correct:
def best_sort(a):
    return sorted(a)
Complexity: O(n) to O(n log n)

