Ruby · queues · patterns · L2
Concept: A moving average keeps a queue of the window and divides by its current length
Misconception: Dividing the running sum by the window size is right from the first value.
Explanation: Until the window fills, the queue holds fewer values than the window size, so dividing by the size understates the average. Add the new value, subtract the value that leaves the queue, and divide by the queue length. fdiv avoids integer division. Each update is O(1).
Incorrect:
class MovingBad
  def initialize(n)
    @n = n
    @q = []
    @sum = 0
  end
  def add(v)
    @q.push(v)
    @sum += v
    @sum -= @q.shift if @q.size > @n
    @sum.fdiv(@n)
  end
end
Correct:
class MovingAverage
  def initialize(n)
    @n = n
    @q = []
    @sum = 0
  end
  def add(v)
    @q.push(v)
    @sum += v
    @sum -= @q.shift if @q.size > @n
    @sum.fdiv(@q.size)
  end
end
Complexity: O(1)

