Ruby · Queue and SizedQueue (thread-safe queues) · patterns · L3
Concept: Close the queue to stop all workers; a single sentinel value stops only one of them
Misconception: Pushing one :done value shuts down every worker.
Explanation: Each :done is consumed by exactly one worker, so with two workers one sentinel leaves the other blocked forever in pop. Queue#close wakes every waiting consumer: pop returns nil once a closed queue is empty, so workers can loop with while (job = q.pop). After close, push raises ClosedQueueError.
Incorrect:
def finished_bad(workers)
  q = Queue.new
  threads = Array.new(workers) { Thread.new { while (j = q.pop) != :done; end } }
  3.times { |i| q << i }
  q << :done
  count = threads.count { |t| t.join(0.2) }
  threads.each(&:kill)
  count
end
Correct:
def finished(workers)
  q = Queue.new
  threads = Array.new(workers) { Thread.new { while (j = q.pop); end } }
  3.times { |i| q << i }
  q.close
  count = threads.count { |t| t.join(0.2) }
  threads.each(&:kill)
  count
end
Complexity: O(1)

