TypeScript · arraybuffer · equality · L2
Concept: Two ArrayBuffers are equal only if you compare their bytes; === checks identity
Misconception: a === b is true for buffers holding the same bytes.
Explanation: ArrayBuffer is an object, so === and == test identity. Compare byteLength first, then every byte through a Uint8Array view. In Node, Buffer.compare or buffer.equals does the same.
Incorrect:
function sameBad(a: ArrayBuffer, b: ArrayBuffer): boolean {
  return a === b;
}
Correct:
function same(a: ArrayBuffer, b: ArrayBuffer): boolean {
  if (a.byteLength !== b.byteLength) return false;
  const x = new Uint8Array(a);
  const y = new Uint8Array(b);
  for (let i = 0; i < x.length; i++) if (x[i] !== y[i]) return false;
  return true;
}
Complexity: O(n)

