document:
TypeScript · arraybuffer · mutation · L1
Concept: Several views over one ArrayBuffer share the same bytes; new Uint8Array(view) copies but new Uint8Array(view.buffer) does not
Misconception: new Uint8Array(u.buffer) makes an independent copy of u.
Explanation: A view is a window onto the buffer. A second view on the same buffer sees every write. Passing a typed array to a constructor copies its elements, but passing its .buffer shares the memory (and ignores the original offset and length). Use u.slice() for an independent copy.
Incorrect:
function copyBad(u: Uint8Array): Uint8Array {
  return new Uint8Array(u.buffer);
}
Correct:
function copy(u: Uint8Array): Uint8Array {
  return u.slice();
}
Complexity: O(n)

