TypeScript · bloomfilter · access · L2
Concept: When packing bits into bytes, shift by i & 7; shifting by i loses bits above the byte
Misconception: bytes[i >> 3] |= 1 << i packs bit i into its byte.
Explanation: A byte holds bits 0 to 7. The shift 1 << i is taken modulo 32, so for i = 9 it is 512, which does not fit in a Uint8Array element and is stored as 0, silently dropping the bit. Use 1 << (i & 7) for the position inside the byte and i >> 3 for the byte index. Packing divides memory by 8.
Incorrect:
function setBitBad(bits: Uint8Array, i: number): void {
  bits[i >> 3] |= 1 << i;
}
Correct:
function setBit(bits: Uint8Array, i: number): void {
  bits[i >> 3] |= 1 << (i & 7);
}
function getBit(bits: Uint8Array, i: number): boolean {
  return ((bits[i >> 3] as number) & (1 << (i & 7))) !== 0;
}
Complexity: O(1)

