document:
TypeScript · btree · mental-model · L1
Concept: With minimum degree t a node holds t-1 to 2t-1 keys; a node with 2t keys cannot split evenly
Misconception: A node may hold up to 2t keys.
Explanation: A full node holds 2t-1 keys. Splitting it moves the median key up and leaves two nodes of t-1 keys each, because 2(t-1) + 1 = 2t-1. A node of 2t keys has no single median, so the split would be uneven. Non-root nodes keep at least t-1 keys and internal nodes have between t and 2t children.
Incorrect:
function limitsBad(t: number): { min: number; max: number; maxChildren: number } {
  return { min: t - 1, max: 2 * t, maxChildren: 2 * t + 1 };
}
Correct:
function limits(t: number): { min: number; max: number; maxChildren: number } {
  return { min: t - 1, max: 2 * t - 1, maxChildren: 2 * t };
}
Complexity: O(1)

