TypeScript · dataview · access · L2
Concept: getBigInt64 returns a bigint; adding a number is error TS2365, so write 1n
Misconception: A 64-bit read returns a number you can add 1 to.
Explanation: A JavaScript number cannot hold every 64-bit integer, so getBigInt64 and getBigUint64 return bigint. Mixing bigint with number in arithmetic is error TS2365 in the compiler and TypeError at run time. Use bigint literals (1n) and convert deliberately with Number(x) when the value is small.
