Concept: Reading past the end of a DataView throws RangeError instead of returning undefined
Misconception: dv.getUint32(offset) returns undefined past the end, like an array.
Explanation: DataView methods throw RangeError when offset + size exceeds byteLength. Check the bounds first and return a safe value. This is the main difference from a typed array, where an out-of-range index gives undefined.
