Concept: When a typed array is a window onto a larger buffer, build the DataView with its byteOffset and byteLength
Misconception: new DataView(u.buffer) views the same bytes as the Uint8Array u.
Explanation: A subarray or a Node Buffer often shares a larger underlying buffer, starting at byteOffset. new DataView(u.buffer) starts at the beginning of that buffer, so every offset is wrong. Pass u.byteOffset and u.byteLength.
Incorrect:
function viewBad(u: Uint8Array): DataView {
  return new DataView(u.buffer);
}
Correct:
function view(u: Uint8Array): DataView {
  return new DataView(u.buffer, u.byteOffset, u.byteLength);
}
Complexity: O(1)

