document:
TypeScript · date · edge-cases · L2
Concept: Adding a month to January 31 overflows into March; clamp the day to the end of the target month
Misconception: setUTCMonth(m + 1) on Jan 31 gives Feb 29 or Feb 28.
Explanation: When the day does not exist in the target month, Date rolls forward: Jan 31 plus one month becomes March 2 or 3. For billing and calendars you usually want the last day of the target month. Compute the target month length with Date.UTC(y, m + 1, 0) and take the smaller day.
Incorrect:
function addMonthsBad(d: Date, n: number): Date {
  const r = new Date(d);
  r.setUTCMonth(r.getUTCMonth() + n);
  return r;
}
Correct:
function addMonths(d: Date, n: number): Date {
  const y = d.getUTCFullYear();
  const m = d.getUTCMonth() + n;
  const last = new Date(Date.UTC(y, m + 1, 0)).getUTCDate();
  return new Date(Date.UTC(y, m, Math.min(d.getUTCDate(), last)));
}
Complexity: O(1)

