Concept: peekFront and peekBack return T | undefined, so using the result directly is error TS2532
Misconception: The front element of a deque of numbers can be used without a check.
Explanation: An empty deque has no front, so the return type includes undefined. Calling a method on it is error TS2532. Test size first, or use optional chaining (d.peekFront()?.toFixed(1)).
Incorrect (compile error TS2532):
function fixedBad(d: Deque<number>): string {
  return d.peekFront().toFixed(1);
}
Correct:
function fixed(d: Deque<number>): string | undefined {
  return d.peekFront()?.toFixed(1);
}
Complexity: O(1)

