TypeScript · deque · patterns · L3
Concept: 0-1 BFS puts zero-weight neighbours at the front and must not mark a node final when it is first reached
Misconception: Marking a node seen when it is first discovered gives shortest distances.
Explanation: With edge weights 0 and 1 a node can be reached first by a weight-1 edge and later by a cheaper path of zero-weight edges. Marking it seen on discovery freezes the worse distance. Use the distance array as the check (relax when strictly better), pushFront for weight 0 and pushBack for weight 1. Total work stays O(V + E).
Incorrect:
function zeroOneBad(adj: [number, number][][], src: number): number[] {
  const dist = adj.map(() => Infinity);
  const seen = new Set<number>([src]);
