TypeScript · directedgraph · creation · L1
Concept: Build the adjacency list with Array.from; fill([]) shares one inner array between all vertices
Misconception: new Array(n).fill([]) creates n empty neighbour lists.
Explanation: fill puts the same array object in every slot. Adding a neighbour to one vertex adds it to all of them. Create a separate array for each vertex with Array.from({ length: n }, () => []), which calls the factory once per slot.
Incorrect:
function makeBad(n: number): number[][] {
  return new Array(n).fill([]) as number[][];
}
Correct:
class DiGraph {
  adj: number[][];
  constructor(readonly n: number) {
    this.adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => [] as number[]);
  }
  addEdge(u: number, v: number): void {
    (this.adj[u] as number[]).push(v);
  }
}
Complexity: O(V)

