TypeScript · disjointset · access · L1
Concept: find must follow parents all the way to the root; returning the direct parent is only correct for depth one
Misconception: find(x) can return parent[x], since that is the set representative.
Explanation: The representative of a set is its root, the element that is its own parent. After several unions an element may be several levels below the root, so a single hop returns an intermediate node and two members of one set compare as different. Loop until parent[x] === x.
Incorrect:
function findBad(parent: number[], x: number): number {
  return parent[x] as number;
}
Correct:
function find(parent: number[], x: number): number {
  while (parent[x] !== x) x = parent[x] as number;
  return x;
}
Complexity: O(depth)

