TypeScript · disjointset · mutation · L1
Concept: union must link the roots of the two sets, not the two elements
Misconception: parent[a] = b merges the sets of a and b.
Explanation: Linking a to b overwrites the parent pointer of a, which may have been linking a to its own set. Elements that reached the root through a are cut off. Find both roots first and attach one root under the other.
Incorrect:
function unionBad(parent: number[], a: number, b: number): void {
  parent[a] = b;
}
Correct:
function union(parent: number[], a: number, b: number): void {
  parent[find(parent, a)] = find(parent, b);
}
Complexity: O(depth)

