TypeScript · enum · access · L1
Concept: A string enum has no reverse mapping; looking up a member by its value needs a search, not Dir[value]
Misconception: Dir["UP"] returns the member name for the value "UP".
Explanation: Only numeric members get a reverse mapping. Indexing a string enum with a value string is error TS7053. To find the member name of a value, search Object.entries, or build the reverse map once.
Incorrect (compile error TS7053):
enum DirB { Up = "UP", Down = "DOWN" }
function nameOfBad(v: string): string {
  return DirB[v];
}
Correct:
enum Dir { Up = "UP", Down = "DOWN" }
function nameOf(v: string): string | undefined {
  return Object.entries(Dir).find(([, val]) => val === v)?.[0];
}
Complexity: O(n)

