TypeScript · fenwicktree · mental-model · L1
Concept: x & -x isolates the lowest set bit, which is the size of the range a node covers
Misconception: The lowest set bit of x can be found with x % 2 or x & 1.
Explanation: A Fenwick node at 1-based index x stores the sum of the lowbit(x) elements ending at x. lowbit(x) is the value of the lowest set bit, computed as x & -x using two's complement. x % 2 and x & 1 only report whether the lowest bit is set, so they return 0 or 1, never 4 or 8.
Incorrect:
function lowbitBad(x: number): number {
  return x & 1;
}
Correct:
function lowbit(x: number): number {
  return x & -x;
}
Complexity: O(1)

