TypeScript · fenwicktree · access · L2
Concept: A range sum subtracts the prefix before l, so it uses l - 1
Misconception: sum(l, r) = prefix(r) - prefix(l).
Explanation: prefix(l) includes element l, so subtracting it removes the first element of the range. The correct difference is prefix(r) - prefix(l - 1). For l = 0 the argument is -1, which makes the walk start at 0 and return 0, so no special case is needed.
Incorrect:
function rangeBad(f: Fenwick, l: number, r: number): number {
  return f.prefix(r) - f.prefix(l);
}
Correct:
function rangeSum(f: Fenwick, l: number, r: number): number {
  return f.prefix(r) - f.prefix(l - 1);
}
Complexity: O(log n)

