TypeScript · fenwicktree · patterns · L3
Concept: Range add with point query stores differences, so the range end must cancel the start
Misconception: Adding d at l alone adds d to the range [l, r].
Explanation: Store a difference array in the tree. A point query is the prefix sum of differences. Adding d at l raises every later position, so a matching -d at r + 1 is needed to end the range. Without it the change leaks to the end of the array.
Incorrect:
class RangeAddBad {
  f: Fenwick;
  constructor(n: number) { this.f = new Fenwick(n); }
  rangeAdd(l: number, r: number, d: number): void {
    this.f.add(l, d);
  }
  get(i: number): number { return this.f.prefix(i); }
}
Correct:
class RangeAdd {
  f: Fenwick;
  constructor(n: number) { this.f = new Fenwick(n); }
  rangeAdd(l: number, r: number, d: number): void {
    this.f.add(l, d);
    this.f.add(r + 1, -d);
  }
  get(i: number): number { return this.f.prefix(i); }
}
Complexity: O(log n)

