TypeScript · interface · insertion-and-deletion · L2
Concept: An interface that extends another cannot change a property to an incompatible type (TS2430)
Misconception: A child interface may redefine a property with any type.
Explanation: A property in the child must be assignable to the parent property of the same name, otherwise error TS2430. Narrowing is allowed (string to "a" | "b"); widening or changing the type is not. To change a type, use Omit and add the property back.
Incorrect (compile error TS2430):
interface BaseB { id: number }
interface ChildB extends BaseB { id: string }
Correct:
interface Base { id: number }
interface Child extends Omit<Base, "id"> { id: string }
function idOf(c: Child): string {
  return c.id;
}
Complexity: O(1)

