TypeScript · interface · mutation · L1
Concept: A readonly property cannot be assigned (TS2540), but the check is compile-time only
Misconception: readonly in an interface prevents changes at run time.
Explanation: Assigning to a readonly property is error TS2540. The modifier is erased, so a cast or plain JavaScript can still write to it, and a mutable alias of the same object can change it. Use Object.freeze when the guarantee must hold at run time.
Incorrect (compile error TS2540):
function renameBad(u: { readonly name: string }): void {
  u.name = "x";
}
Correct:
interface User { readonly name: string }
function renamed(u: User, name: string): User {
  return { ...u, name };
}
Complexity: O(1)

