Concept: Prepending must point the new node at the old head; pointing at null drops the rest of the list
Misconception: A new head node can be created with next set to null and the old list reattached later.
Explanation: If the new node does not reference the old head, every old node becomes unreachable and the list silently has one element. The correct insertion links first (new.next = head) and then moves the head, in O(1).
