TypeScript · map · transformation · L2
Concept: Map.groupBy builds Map<K, T[]> in one call; hand-written grouping must create the array before pushing
Misconception: m.get(key).push(x) works for every key once the Map is created.
Explanation: A new Map has no arrays, so get returns undefined for the first item of each group and push throws TypeError. Create the bucket on first use, or call Map.groupBy(items, fn), which returns a Map of arrays in first-seen key order.
Incorrect:
function groupBad(xs: readonly number[]): Map<boolean, number[]> {
  const m = new Map<boolean, number[]>();
  for (const x of xs) m.get(x % 2 === 0)!.push(x);
  return m;
}
Correct:
function group(xs: readonly number[]): Map<boolean, number[]> {
  return Map.groupBy(xs, (x) => x % 2 === 0);
}
Complexity: O(n)

