TypeScript · map · iteration · L2
Concept: Entries added during iteration are visited; iterate over a snapshot when you add keys
Misconception: A for...of loop over a Map sees only the entries that existed when the loop began.
Explanation: Map iteration is live. Deleting the current entry is safe, but a key added during the loop is visited later, so a loop that adds a key per entry never ends. Copy first with [...m] when you need to add or reorder.
Incorrect:
function spreadBad(m: Map<number, number>): number {
  let visits = 0;
  for (const [k, v] of m) {
    visits++;
    if (visits > 50) break;
    m.set(k + 1, v);
  }
  return visits;
}
Correct:
function spread(m: Map<number, number>): number {
  let visits = 0;
  for (const [k, v] of [...m]) {
    visits++;
    m.set(k + 1, v);
  }
  return visits;
}
Complexity: O(n)

