TypeScript · map · fit-and-alternatives · L2
Concept: JSON.stringify(map) gives "{}"; convert with [...map] or Object.fromEntries first
Misconception: JSON.stringify serialises a Map like any other collection.
Explanation: A Map has no enumerable own properties, so JSON.stringify returns "{}" and the data is lost silently. Serialise [...map] (an array of pairs) and rebuild with new Map(pairs). Object.fromEntries works when all keys are strings.
Incorrect:
function saveBad(m: Map<string, number>): string {
  return JSON.stringify(m);
}
Correct:
function save(m: Map<string, number>): string {
  return JSON.stringify([...m]);
}
function load(s: string): Map<string, number> {
  return new Map(JSON.parse(s) as [string, number][]);
}
Complexity: O(n)

