Concept: A queue with a head index is O(1) per dequeue, but size must subtract the head offset
Misconception: The size of an index-based queue is items.length.
Explanation: Array.shift is O(n) because every element moves. A head index avoids that: dequeue reads items[head] and advances. The live length is then items.length - head, not items.length. Counting consumed slots makes isEmpty false forever. Mnemonist (npm) has a Queue class with the same operations.
