Concept: Record<number, V> still has string keys at run time; Object.keys gives strings
Misconception: Object.keys of a Record<number, string> returns numbers.
Explanation: Object keys are always strings or symbols. The number key 5 is stored as "5", and Object.keys returns ["5"]. Comparing or searching with a number is error TS2345 (and false at run time). Convert with Number(k) or String(n), or use a Map<number, V> for real numeric keys.
