TypeScript · redblacktree · mutation · L2
Concept: A colour flip toggles the parent and both children, which splits a temporary 4-node
Misconception: A flip toggles the two children only.
Explanation: A node with two red children represents a temporary 4-node. Flipping turns both children black and the parent red, which sends the extra red link up one level without changing any black height. Toggling only the children changes the black height of the paths below and breaks the invariant.
Incorrect:
function flipBad<K>(h: RbNode<K>): void {
  const l = h.left as RbNode<K>;
  const r = h.right as RbNode<K>;
  l.color = !l.color;
  r.color = !r.color;
}
Correct:
function flip<K>(h: RbNode<K>): void {
  const l = h.left as RbNode<K>;
  const r = h.right as RbNode<K>;
  h.color = !h.color;
  l.color = !l.color;
  r.color = !r.color;
}
Complexity: O(1)

