TypeScript · redblacktree · mutation · L2
Concept: The public insert paints the root black after every insertion
Misconception: insert already returns a valid tree.
Explanation: The recursive insert may leave a red root, for example after a flip at the top or for the first key. A red root is not allowed, and it also makes the black height of the root ambiguous. The wrapper sets the root black after every insert.
Incorrect:
function putBad<K>(root: RbNode<K> | null, key: K, cmp: Cmp<K>): RbNode<K> {
  return insert(root, key, cmp);
}
Correct:
function put<K>(root: RbNode<K> | null, key: K, cmp: Cmp<K>): RbNode<K> {
  const r = insert(root, key, cmp);
  r.color = BLACK;
  return r;
}
Complexity: O(log n)

