TypeScript · regexp · mutation · L2
Concept: A regex with the g or y flag keeps lastIndex between test() calls, so repeated calls can alternate
Misconception: A shared regex can be reused for every test() call without side effects.
Explanation: With the g flag, test and exec start at lastIndex and update it after a match. The same regex tested twice against the same string returns true then false. Use a regex without g for plain tests, create it inside the function, or reset lastIndex to 0.
Incorrect:
const VOWEL = /[aeiou]/g;
function hasVowelBad(s: string): boolean {
  return VOWEL.test(s);
}
Correct:
const VOWEL_OK = /[aeiou]/;
function hasVowel(s: string): boolean {
  return VOWEL_OK.test(s);
}
Complexity: O(n)

