TypeScript · regexp · iteration · L1
Concept: matchAll requires the g flag; without it the call throws TypeError at runtime
Misconception: str.matchAll(re) returns every match for any regex.
Explanation: matchAll throws TypeError when the regex lacks the g flag. The compiler cannot see flags, so this passes type checking. Add g, or call exec once. The result is an iterator, so spread it with [...] or loop over it.
Incorrect:
function digitsBad(s: string): string[] {
  return [...s.matchAll(/\d/)].map((m) => m[0]);
}
Correct:
function digits(s: string): string[] {
  return [...s.matchAll(/\d/g)].map((m) => m[0]);
}
Complexity: O(n)

