document:
TypeScript · set · equality · L1
Concept: Set removes duplicates by SameValueZero, so equal-looking objects all stay; dedupe objects by a primitive key
Misconception: new Set(points) removes points that have the same x and y.
Explanation: A Set compares objects by reference. Two literals with the same fields are different members, so the duplicates remain. Build a string or number key (for example `${x},${y}`) and track seen keys, or store only keys.
Incorrect:
function dedupeBad(ps: { x: number; y: number }[]): { x: number; y: number }[] {
  return [...new Set(ps)];
}
Correct:
function dedupe(ps: { x: number; y: number }[]): { x: number; y: number }[] {
  const seen = new Set<string>();
  return ps.filter((p) => {
    const key = `${p.x},${p.y}`;
    if (seen.has(key)) return false;
    seen.add(key);
    return true;
  });
}
Complexity: O(n)

