TypeScript · set · ordering · L1
Concept: A Set iterates in insertion order and is not sorted; sort the spread array when you need order
Misconception: [...new Set(xs)] returns the values in ascending order.
Explanation: A Set remembers first insertion order only. Adding an existing value changes nothing. To get sorted output, spread to an array and sort with a numeric comparator, because the default sort compares strings.
Incorrect:
function sortedBad(xs: readonly number[]): number[] {
  return [...new Set(xs)];
}
Correct:
function sorted(xs: readonly number[]): number[] {
  return [...new Set(xs)].sort((a, b) => a - b);
}
Complexity: O(n log n)

