TypeScript · set · access · L0
Concept: A Set has size, not length, and no index access; spread to an array when you need either
Misconception: A Set can be measured with s.length and read with s[0].
Explanation: Set exposes size and has/add/delete. Reading s.length is error TS2339 in TypeScript and undefined in plain JavaScript. There is no index access either. Use s.size for the count and [...s] or an iterator for positional access.
Incorrect (compile error TS2339):
function sizeBad(s: Set<number>): number {
  return s.length;
}
Correct:
function sizeOf(s: ReadonlySet<number>): number {
  return s.size;
}
function firstOf(s: ReadonlySet<number>): number | undefined {
  return s.values().next().value;
}
Complexity: O(1)

