TypeScript · set · equality · L2
Concept: isSubsetOf tests membership of every element; comparing sizes is not a subset test
Misconception: a is a subset of b whenever a.size <= b.size.
Explanation: A smaller set need not be contained in the larger one. Use a.isSubsetOf(b), isSupersetOf or isDisjointFrom. Two sets are equal when their sizes match and one is a subset of the other.
Incorrect:
function isSubsetBad(a: ReadonlySet<number>, b: ReadonlySet<number>): boolean {
  return a.size <= b.size;
}
Correct:
function isSubset(a: ReadonlySet<number>, b: ReadonlySet<number>): boolean {
  return a.isSubsetOf(b);
}
Complexity: O(n)

