TypeScript · trie · iteration · L2
Concept: Iterate a word with for...of; an index loop splits characters outside the basic plane
Misconception: word.length and word[i] walk the characters of a word.
Explanation: A string is a sequence of UTF-16 code units. Characters such as emoji take two units, so indexing or split("") cuts them into halves and the trie stores meaningless nodes. for...of and the spread operator iterate whole code points.
Incorrect:
function unitsBad(word: string): string[] {
  return word.split("");
}
Correct:
function codePoints(word: string): string[] {
  return [...word];
}
Complexity: O(L)

