TypeScript · typealias · patterns · L2
Concept: satisfies checks a value against a type without widening it; an annotation hides the literal members
Misconception: Annotating with Record<string, string | number> keeps cfg.port typed as number.
Explanation: An annotation replaces the inferred type, so cfg.port becomes string | number and calling toFixed is error TS2339. The satisfies operator validates the shape but keeps the precise inferred type, so cfg.port stays number.
Incorrect (compile error TS2339):
const cfgB: Record<string, string | number> = { port: 80 };
const bad = cfgB.port.toFixed(1);
