TypeScript · typedarray · insertion-and-deletion · L1
Concept: A typed array has a fixed length and no push, pop or splice; allocate a new array and set
Misconception: A typed array grows with push like a normal array.
Explanation: The length of a typed array is fixed at creation. push is error TS2339 and a TypeError in JavaScript. To append, allocate a longer array, copy with set(), and write the new element. For many appends collect values in a normal array first, or use a growable ArrayBuffer.
Incorrect (compile error TS2339):
function appendBad(u: Uint8Array, x: number): Uint8Array {
  u.push(x);
  return u;
}
Correct:
function append(u: Uint8Array, x: number): Uint8Array {
  const r = new Uint8Array(u.length + 1);
  r.set(u);
  r[u.length] = x;
  return r;
}
Complexity: O(n)

