Concept: Integer typed arrays wrap on overflow and truncate decimals; Uint8ClampedArray clamps to 0-255 and rounds
Misconception: Storing 300 in a Uint8Array stores 255, the nearest valid value.
Explanation: Uint8Array keeps the value modulo 256: 300 becomes 44 and -5 becomes 251. Fractions are truncated. Uint8ClampedArray clamps to 0..255 and rounds half to even, so it is the right type for colours and pixel data. Int8, Int16, Int32 and their unsigned versions wrap in the same way.
