Concept: Count a component only for a start vertex that has not been visited yet
Misconception: Every vertex is the start of a new component.
Explanation: The outer loop visits all vertices as possible start points. A vertex already reached by an earlier traversal belongs to a component that was already counted. Skip visited starts before incrementing the counter, otherwise the result is the number of vertices.
