TypeScript · weakmap · iteration · L1
Concept: A WeakMap has no size, keys or forEach; track counts yourself or use a Map
Misconception: A WeakMap can be listed and counted like a Map.
Explanation: Entries can disappear whenever the garbage collector runs, so the API hides them: only get, set, has and delete exist. Reading size is error TS2339 and undefined at runtime. If you need to list or count entries, use a Map and manage removal yourself.
Incorrect (compile error TS2339):
function countBad(wm: WeakMap<object, number>): number {
  return wm.size;
}
Correct:
function countKeys(m: ReadonlyMap<object, number>): number {
  return m.size;
}
Complexity: O(1)

