TypeScript · weakmap · edge-cases · L3
Concept: Symbol.for symbols are registered and cannot be WeakMap keys; Symbol() symbols can
Misconception: Any symbol is allowed as a WeakMap key.
Explanation: Since ES2023 a WeakMap accepts symbols that are not in the global registry. Symbol("x") is fine, but Symbol.for("x") can never be collected, so using it as a key throws TypeError. The compiler types both as symbol, so this error only appears at runtime.
Incorrect:
function setRegisteredBad(wm: WeakMap<symbol, number>, n: number): void {
  wm.set(Symbol.for("k"), n);
}
Correct:
function setLocal(wm: WeakMap<symbol, number>, n: number): symbol {
  const key = Symbol("k");
  wm.set(key, n);
  return key;
}
Complexity: O(1)

