TypeScript · weakset · iteration · L1
Concept: A WeakSet has only add, has and delete; there is no size, no iteration and no clear
Misconception: A WeakSet can report how many objects it holds.
Explanation: Because members may be collected at any time, the API hides them. Reading size is error TS2339 and undefined at runtime. If you need a count or a listing, use a Set and remove members yourself.
Incorrect (compile error TS2339):
function sizeBad(ws: WeakSet<object>): number {
  return ws.size;
}
Correct:
function sizeOfSet(s: ReadonlySet<object>): number {
  return s.size;
}
Complexity: O(1)

