TypeScript · weakset · mutation · L2
Concept: Track "already processed" objects in a WeakSet instead of adding a flag property to them
Misconception: Setting a processed flag on the object is a safe way to remember it.
Explanation: A flag property mutates inputs, appears in JSON and copies, and throws TypeError in strict mode when the object is frozen. A module-level WeakSet records membership outside the object, works on frozen objects, and forgets the object when it is collected.
Incorrect:
function initOnceBad(o: { n: number }): boolean {
  const x = o as { n: number; done?: boolean };
  if (x.done) return false;
  x.done = true;
  return true;
}
Correct:
const done = new WeakSet<object>();
function initOnce(o: object): boolean {
  if (done.has(o)) return false;
  done.add(o);
  return true;
}
Complexity: O(1)

