TypeScript · weightedgraph · creation · L1
Concept: Type each edge as a [to, weight] tuple so the compiler rejects an edge without a weight
Misconception: An edge can be pushed as [v] and the weight added later.
Explanation: A weighted adjacency list stores pairs. Typing the pair as a tuple [to: number, w: number] makes the compiler reject a push of [v] with TS2345, which would otherwise create an edge with an undefined weight and produce NaN distances later. Array.from builds one list per vertex.
Incorrect (compile error TS2345):
type EdgeB = [to: number, w: number];
function addBad(adj: EdgeB[][], u: number, v: number): void {
  (adj[u] as EdgeB[]).push([v]);
}
Correct:
type Edge = [to: number, w: number];
class WGraph {
  adj: Edge[][];
  constructor(readonly n: number) {
    this.adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => [] as Edge[]);
  }
  addEdge(u: number, v: number, w: number): void {
    (this.adj[u] as Edge[]).push([v, w]);
  }
}
Complexity: O(1)

