TypeScript Weighted Graph: Training Data for the DSA Mentor RAG Chatbot
Page 1
TypeScript Weighted Graph
A training document for the DSA Mentor RAG collection. It teaches the weighted graph in TypeScript with
a WGraph class and an Edge tuple type: tuple-typed edges, undirected edges, Dijkstra, Bellman-Ford with
negative cycle detection, Prim's minimum spanning tree and Floyd-Warshall. JavaScript and Mnemonist
have no graph class, so it is written here.
13 October 2026. Every example in this document was executed in TypeScript 5.9 (strict mode) on Node 22: 6 concept chunks and 6
exercises, with 12 test runs and 0 failures. Concept chunks carry verified: true in the export.
Built for retrieval. Each concept card is one RAG chunk (one misconception, one explanation, one failing and one
passing example) and each exercise is one more. The algorithms and strategies live in their own section (4) and are
tagged section: algorithms-and-strategies in the metadata, so the mentor can filter to them.
