TypeScript Segment Tree: Training Data for the DSA Mentor RAG Chatbot
Page 1
TypeScript Segment Tree
A training document for the DSA Mentor RAG collection. It teaches the segment tree in TypeScript:
recursive build with 4n slots, range sum queries, point updates, an iterative bottom-up min tree with the
correct identity and half-open ranges, and lazy propagation for range adds. Mnemonist has no segment
tree, so the classes are written here.
13 October 2026. Every example in this document was executed in TypeScript 5.9 (strict mode) on Node 22: 7 concept chunks and 5
exercises, with 11 test runs and 0 failures. Concept chunks carry verified: true in the export.
Built for retrieval. Each concept card is one RAG chunk (one misconception, one explanation, one failing and one
passing example) and each exercise is one more. The algorithms and strategies live in their own section (4) and are
tagged section: algorithms-and-strategies in the metadata, so the mentor can filter to them.
