explanation.
The public insert paints the root black after every insertion
ts-redblacktree-root-black   lens: mutation   level: L2   family: ts-rb-mutation
Prerequisites: ts-redblacktree-fixup. Follow-up: ts-redblacktree-checker. Complexity: O(log n).
Common misconception. insert already returns a valid tree.
The recursive insert may leave a red root, for example after a flip at the top or for the first key. A red root is not
allowed, and it also makes the black height of the root ambiguous. The wrapper sets the root black after every insert.
Incorrect (runs, but fails as described):
function putBad<K>(root: RbNode<K> | null, key: K, cmp: Cmp<K>): RbNode<K> {
return insert(root, key, cmp);
}
Correct:
function put<K>(root: RbNode<K> | null, key: K, cmp: Cmp<K>): RbNode<K> {
const r = insert(root, key, cmp);
r.color = BLACK;
return r;
}

