TypeScript Doubly Linked List
A training document for the DSA Mentor RAG collection. It teaches a doubly linked list in TypeScript with a
generic DNode: two-way links, head and tail edge cases, O(1) node removal, insertion, reversal and an
LRU cache built with a Map. Mnemonist (npm) offers a LinkedList class; the pointer logic here is what
interviews ask you to write.
13 October 2026. Every example in this document was executed in TypeScript 5.9 (strict mode) on Node 22: 6 concept chunks and 5
exercises, with 9 test runs and 0 failures. Concept chunks carry verified: true in the export.
Built for retrieval. Each concept card is one RAG chunk (one misconception, one explanation, one failing and one
passing example) and each exercise is one more. The algorithms and strategies live in their own section (4) and are
tagged section: algorithms-and-strategies in the metadata, so the mentor can filter to them.
